description_COLLECTIVE_1 = "**Strategy: Generous Threshold Reciprocity (GTR)**\n\nLet m_t = number of opponents (out of n\u22121) who cooperated in round t. Define the cooperation threshold T = \u2308(n\u22121) \u00d7 (k\u22121)/k\u2309 \u2014 the minimum number of cooperating opponents that makes mutual cooperation collectively worthwhile relative to defection cascades. Maintain a \"goodwill\" counter g, initialized to 2.\n\n**Round 0:** Cooperate.\n\n**Rounds 1 to r\u22122:** After observing m_{t\u22121}:\n\n1. Update goodwill:\n   - If m_{t\u22121} \u2265 T: g \u2190 min(g + 1, 3)\n   - Else: g \u2190 g \u2212 1\n2. Decision:\n   - If m_{t\u22121} \u2265 T: play C.\n   - Else if g > 0: play C (generous forgiveness \u2014 absorb up to a few bad rounds to avoid noise-driven collapse).\n   - Else: play D.\n3. Recovery probe: if defecting and it has been at least 3 consecutive rounds of D, play C once with probability 1/2 (or deterministically every 4th D-round) to test whether the group can re-coordinate. If the probe finds m \u2265 T, reset g \u2190 2 and resume cooperation.\n\n**Last round (t = r\u22121):** \n- If m_{r\u22122} \u2265 n\u22122 (near-full cooperation) play C \u2014 preserve full-group surplus and reward reliable cooperators; otherwise play D.\n\n**Edge cases:**\n- If r = 2: cooperate round 0; in round 1 cooperate only if all opponents cooperated.\n- If T = 0 (very high k relative to n), always cooperate except apply the last-round rule.\n- If every observed round so far had m = 0, set g = 0 permanently and defect (except probes cease after two failed probes).\n\n```\ninit g=2, dstreak=0, failed_probes=0\nfor t in 0..r-1:\n    if t == 0: play C; continue\n    if t == r-1:\n        play C if m[t-1] >= n-2 else D; continue\n    if m[t-1] >= T: g = min(g+1,3); play C; dstreak=0\n    else:\n        g -= 1\n        if g > 0: play C; dstreak=0\n        else:\n            if dstreak >= 3 and failed_probes < 2:\n                play C  # probe\n                if next observed m >= T: g=2 else failed_probes+=1\n                dstreak=0\n            else:\n                play D; dstreak+=1\n```\n\nThe strategy leads with full cooperation, sustains it whenever a critical mass of the group reciprocates, forgives isolated lapses rather than triggering permanent collapse, punishes sustained free-riding by withdrawing contributions, and periodically extends an olive branch to rebuild group cooperation after breakdowns."

description_COLLECTIVE_2 = "**Strategy: Generous Threshold Reciprocation (GTR)**\n\nLet m_t = number of *other* players who cooperated in round t (observed after each round). Define the cooperation threshold T = ceil((n-1) \u00d7 (k-1)/k), roughly the number of co-cooperators needed for cooperation to not be too costly, but never let T exceed ceil((n-1)/2).\n\n**Decision rules:**\n\n1. **Round 0:** Cooperate.\n\n2. **Rounds 1 to r-2:** Cooperate if either:\n   - m_{t-1} \u2265 T (enough others cooperated last round), or\n   - a \"forgiveness probe\" fires: if I've defected for two consecutive rounds, cooperate once to test whether the group can re-coordinate.\n   \n   Otherwise defect.\n\n   Additionally, track a moving signal of momentum: if m decreased for two consecutive rounds and m_{t-1} < T, defect (no probe) \u2014 the group is collapsing; probes resume only after two rounds of defection as above.\n\n3. **Endgame:**\n   - Round r-1 (last round): Defect only if m_{t-1} < n-1 (i.e., anyone defected last round); if all others cooperated in round r-2, cooperate \u2014 reward a fully cooperative group to the end.\n   - Round r-2: Apply the normal rule but raise the threshold to max(T, n-2), guarding against early endgame defection cascades.\n\n**Pseudocode:**\n\n```\nT = min(ceil((n-1)*(k-1)/k), ceil((n-1)/2))\ndefect_streak = 0\n\nfor t in 0..r-1:\n    if t == 0:\n        action = C\n    elif t == r-1:\n        action = C if m[t-1] == n-1 else D\n    elif t == r-2:\n        action = C if m[t-1] >= max(T, n-2) else D\n    else:\n        collapsing = (t >= 2 and m[t-1] < m[t-2] and m[t-1] < T)\n        if m[t-1] >= T and not collapsing:\n            action = C\n        elif defect_streak >= 2:\n            action = C   # forgiveness probe\n        else:\n            action = D\n    defect_streak = 0 if action == C else defect_streak + 1\n    play(action)\n```\n\n**Collective character:** Open with full cooperation to seed mutual contribution; sustain cooperation whenever a viable coalition (\u2265 T others) exists, tolerating some free-riders since group surplus still exceeds all-defect; periodically probe after breakdowns to rebuild cooperation rather than lock into mutual defection; only tighten standards in the final two rounds where reciprocity can no longer be enforced."

description_COLLECTIVE_3 = "**Adaptive Threshold Reciprocation (ATR)**\n\nMaintain: `coop[t]` = number of opponents (out of n\u22121) who cooperated in round t.\n\n**Threshold:** cooperation is collectively worthwhile to sustain when a critical mass exists. Define\n```\nT = ceil((n-1) / 2)        # majority of opponents\n```\n\n**Decision rules:**\n\n1. **Round 0:** Cooperate. Signal willingness to build the public good.\n\n2. **Rounds 1 to r\u22122:**\n   - Compute recent cooperation: `m = coop[t-1]`.\n   - **Cooperate if `m \u2265 T`** (a majority of opponents cooperated last round).\n   - **Forgiveness probe:** if `m < T`, still cooperate once every \u2308r/5\u2309 rounds (i.e., when `t mod ceil(r/5) == 0`), provided at least one opponent cooperated last round (`m \u2265 1`). This tests whether cooperation can be re-established without being endlessly exploited.\n   - **Collapse detection:** if `m = 0` for two consecutive rounds, suspend probes for the next \u2308r/4\u2309 rounds and defect throughout that window.\n   - **Recovery:** any round where `m \u2265 T` immediately resets all suspension counters; resume cooperation next round.\n\n3. **Endgame (last round, t = r\u22121):** Defect only if `coop[r-2] < T`. If the group has sustained majority cooperation into the final round, cooperate \u2014 protecting the cooperative equilibrium against symmetric strategies that also condition endgame play on group health, and avoiding triggering pre-emptive unraveling in earlier rounds against mirror-like opponents.\n\n**Pseudocode:**\n```\nif t == 0: play C\nelif t == r-1:\n    play C if coop[t-1] >= T else D\nelse:\n    if coop[t-1] >= T: play C; clear suspension\n    elif suspended: play D; decrement suspension\n    elif coop[t-1] == 0 and coop[t-2] == 0:\n        suspend for ceil(r/4) rounds; play D\n    elif t % ceil(r/5) == 0 and coop[t-1] >= 1: play C   # probe\n    else: play D\n```\n\nThe strategy starts generous, matches the group's prevailing behavior, periodically extends olive branches to restart cooperation after breakdowns, and withdraws probes only when the group is demonstrably non-cooperative \u2014 maximizing collective surplus whenever a cooperative majority is achievable while limiting losses to persistent defectors."

description_COLLECTIVE_4 = "**Adaptive Threshold Reciprocity**\n\nLet m = n \u2212 1 (number of opponents). Track coop_t = number of opponents who cooperated in round t.\n\nCore threshold: cooperate if enough others are cooperating that mutual cooperation is being sustained. Define T = ceil(m \u00d7 (k\u22121)/k), but at least ceil(m/2) \u2014 i.e., T = max(ceil(m/2), ceil(m\u00b7(k\u22121)/k)).\n\n**Decision rules:**\n\n1. **Round 0:** Cooperate.\n\n2. **Rounds 1 to r\u22122:**\n   - Compute recent cooperation level L = coop_{t\u22121} (last round's opponent cooperators).\n   - Cooperate if L \u2265 T.\n   - **Forgiveness/probe:** If L < T but cooperation is collapsing, attempt periodic revival: cooperate anyway if (t mod p == 0), where p = max(3, round(r/10)). This single-round olive branch tests whether other conditional cooperators will re-coordinate; do not repeat two rounds in a row after a failed probe (i.e., only probe when you defected in the previous round).\n   - **Trend bonus:** Also cooperate if coop_{t\u22121} > coop_{t\u22122} and coop_{t\u22121} \u2265 T \u2212 1 (reward upward momentum near the threshold).\n\n3. **Endgame (last round, t = r\u22121):** Defect only if L < m (i.e., not everyone cooperated last round). If all m opponents cooperated in round r\u22122, cooperate in the final round as well \u2014 sustaining full cooperation among like-minded strategies is worth more across the tournament than a one-shot grab.\n\n4. **Second-to-last round (t = r\u22122):** Apply the normal rule (rule 2), but skip probes \u2014 no time for revival to pay off.\n\n**Pseudocode:**\n\n```\nT = max(ceil((n-1)/2), ceil((n-1)*(k-1)/k))\np = max(3, round(r/10))\n\ndef act(t, history):        # history[t'] = opponent coop count\n    if t == 0: return C\n    L = history[t-1]\n    if t == r-1:\n        return C if L == n-1 else D\n    if L >= T: return C\n    if t >= 2 and history[t-1] > history[t-2] and L >= T-1: return C\n    if t < r-2 and t % p == 0 and my_last_action == D: return C\n    return D\n```\n\nThe strategy opens cooperatively, sustains cooperation whenever a critical mass reciprocates, punishes widespread defection immediately, repeatedly extends recovery signals so groups of conditional cooperators can escape mutual-punishment spirals, and protects the group equilibrium through the final round rather than triggering preemptive endgame unraveling."

description_COLLECTIVE_5 = "**Strategy: Generous Threshold Reciprocation (GTR)**\n\nLet m_t = number of opponents (out of n\u22121) who cooperated in round t. Define the cooperation threshold T = \u2308(n\u22121)/2\u2309 (a majority of opponents).\n\n**Decision rules:**\n\n1. **Round 0:** Cooperate.\n\n2. **Rounds 1 to r\u22122:** Cooperate if m_{t\u22121} \u2265 T; otherwise defect \u2014 **except** apply two overrides:\n   - **Generous probe:** If defecting, still cooperate with probability p = 1/(n\u22121), or deterministically every \u2308n/2\u2309-th consecutive defection round, to test whether cooperation can be restored. If the probe round yields m \u2265 T, resume cooperation.\n   - **Forgiveness after collapse:** If m_{t\u22121} \u2265 T\u22121 and I cooperated in t\u22121 (a near-miss), cooperate again once; if the near-miss repeats twice in a row, switch to the base rule.\n\n3. **Recovery boost:** If a probe or any round shows strictly increasing opponent cooperation for two consecutive rounds (m_t > m_{t\u22121}), cooperate regardless of threshold, to help pull the group back to full cooperation.\n\n4. **Endgame (last round, t = r\u22121):** Cooperate if m_{t\u22121} \u2265 n\u22122 (i.e., opponents were at or near full cooperation); otherwise defect. In round r\u22122, use the normal rule but raise the threshold to T+1 if T+1 \u2264 n\u22121, guarding against early endgame unraveling while still rewarding a strongly cooperative group.\n\n**Pseudocode:**\n\n```\nT = ceil((n-1)/2)\nconsec_defects = 0\n\ndef act(t, history):\n    if t == 0: return C\n    m = history[t-1].opponent_cooperators\n    if t == r-1:\n        return C if m >= n-2 else D\n    thresh = T+1 if (t == r-2 and T+1 <= n-1) else T\n    if m >= thresh or rising_two_rounds(history):\n        consec_defects = 0; return C\n    # near-miss forgiveness\n    if m == thresh-1 and my_last_move == C and not forgave_last_round:\n        return C\n    # generous probe\n    consec_defects += 1\n    if consec_defects % ceil(n/2) == 0:\n        return C\n    return D\n```\n\n**Collective alignment:** The strategy starts trusting, sustains full cooperation as long as a majority reciprocates, forgives single-round noise, and periodically probes to rebuild cooperation after breakdowns \u2014 maximizing the group surplus (k per contributed unit) whenever a critical mass of cooperators exists, while withdrawing contribution only when the group has demonstrably collapsed into exploitation."

description_COLLECTIVE_6 = "**Adaptive Threshold Reciprocity**\n\nLet m = n \u2212 1 (number of opponents). Track coop_t = number of opponents who cooperated in round t.\n\n**Core threshold:** Cooperation is collectively worthwhile to sustain when others reciprocate. Define the reciprocity threshold T = \u2308m \u00d7 (k \u2212 1)/(k)\u2309, but never below \u2308m/2\u2309. Use T* = max(\u2308m/2\u2309, \u2308m(k\u22121)/k\u2309).\n\n**Decision rules:**\n\n1. **Round 0:** Cooperate. Signal willingness to build the public good.\n\n2. **Rounds 1 to r\u22122:** Maintain an exponentially weighted cooperation estimate:\n   - E_0 = coop_0\n   - E_t = 0.6 \u00d7 coop_t + 0.4 \u00d7 E_{t\u22121}\n\n   Then:\n   - If E_{t\u22121} \u2265 T*: **Cooperate.**\n   - If E_{t\u22121} < T*: **Defect**, except apply *forgiveness probes*: cooperate once every \u2308r/10\u2309 rounds (i.e., when t mod \u2308r/10\u2309 == 0) while in the defect state, to test whether the group can be revived \u2014 but only if at least \u2308r \u00d7 0.15\u2309 rounds remain.\n   - **Fast recovery:** if in the defect state and coop_{t\u22121} \u2265 T* (the group rebounded on its own), immediately return to cooperation next round regardless of E.\n\n3. **Generosity buffer:** if coop_{t\u22121} \u2265 T* \u2212 1 and coop_{t\u22122} \u2265 T* (a single-round dip), still cooperate \u2014 don't punish noise.\n\n4. **Endgame:**\n   - **Last round (t = r\u22121):** Defect only if E has been below T* at any point in the last 3 rounds; otherwise cooperate \u2014 reward a fully cooperative group rather than triggering a preemptive unraveling.\n   - **Second-to-last round:** follow the normal rule, but if coop dropped by \u2265 2 from the prior round (others starting endgame defection), defect.\n\n**Pseudocode:**\n\n```\nT = max(ceil((n-1)/2), ceil((n-1)*(k-1)/k))\nprobe_interval = max(2, ceil(r/10))\n\ndef act(t, history):            # history[s] = opponents' coop count in round s\n    if t == 0: return C\n    E = ewma(history, alpha=0.6)\n    last = history[t-1]\n    if t == r-1:\n        return C if all(h >= T for h in history[-3:]) else D\n    if t == r-2 and t >= 2 and history[t-2] - last >= 2:\n        return D\n    if E >= T or last >= T: return C\n    if t >= 2 and last >= T-1 and history[t-2] >= T: return C   # noise tolerance\n    if t % probe_interval == 0 and (r - t) > 0.15*r: return C   # probe\n    return D\n```\n\nThe strategy opens cooperatively, sustains full cooperation whenever a working majority reciprocates, tolerates single-round noise, punishes sustained free-riding quickly, periodically attempts to re-coordinate the group after breakdowns, and avoids initiating endgame defection so that mutually cooperative groups capture the full surplus through the final round."

description_COLLECTIVE_7 = "**Strategy: Generous Threshold Reciprocation with Endgame Guard**\n\nLet m_t = number of opponents (out of n\u22121) who cooperated in round t. Define the cooperation rate \u03c1_t = m_t / (n\u22121), and the threshold \u03b8 = (k\u22121)/(k) capped to lie in [0.4, 0.7] \u2014 i.e., \u03b8 = min(0.7, max(0.4, (k\u22121)/k)).\n\n**Round 0:** Cooperate.\n\n**Rounds 1 to r\u22122:** Maintain a \"goodwill\" state with a forgiveness counter f (start f = 1).\n\n- If \u03c1_{t\u22121} \u2265 \u03b8: Cooperate, and reset f = 1.\n- If \u03c1_{t\u22121} < \u03b8 but \u03c1_{t\u22121} \u2265 \u03b8/2:\n  - If f > 0: Cooperate anyway (spend forgiveness: f \u2190 f\u22121). This probes for recoverable cooperation.\n  - Else: Defect this round, then set f = 1 (so a single cooperative signal from opponents can restore cooperation).\n- If \u03c1_{t\u22121} < \u03b8/2: Defect, set f = 0.\n\n**Recovery probe:** After defecting for 2 consecutive rounds, cooperate once (olive branch) provided at least \u2308r/5\u2309 rounds remain. If the olive branch is met with \u03c1 \u2265 \u03b8/2, resume the normal rule with f = 1; otherwise defect and wait another 2 rounds before probing again.\n\n**Endgame:**\n- Round r\u22121 (last round): Defect only if \u03c1 over the last 3 rounds averaged below \u03b8; otherwise cooperate \u2014 sustaining mutual cooperation to the end rewards cooperative populations and avoids triggering cascade unraveling against reciprocators.\n- Round r\u22122: Play the normal rule (no early defection).\n\n**Edge cases:**\n- If n\u22121 = 1, treat as generous tit-for-tat: cooperate iff opponent cooperated last round, forgiving one defection per two rounds, cooperate in the final round if the opponent cooperated last round.\n- If r \u2264 3: cooperate round 0, then cooperate iff \u03c1_{t\u22121} \u2265 \u03b8.\n\nPseudocode:\n\n```\n\u03b8 = clamp((k-1)/k, 0.4, 0.7); f = 1; defect_streak = 0\nfor t in 0..r-1:\n    if t == 0: play C; continue\n    if t == r-1:\n        play C if mean(\u03c1 over last min(3,t) rounds) \u2265 \u03b8 else D; continue\n    if defect_streak >= 2 and remaining_rounds \u2265 ceil(r/5):\n        play C  # olive branch\n    elif \u03c1_{t-1} \u2265 \u03b8: play C; f = 1\n    elif \u03c1_{t-1} \u2265 \u03b8/2:\n        if f > 0: play C; f -= 1\n        else: play D; f = 1\n    else: play D; f = 0\n    update defect_streak (0 if played C, else +1)\n```\n\nThe strategy opens cooperatively, tolerates noise and partial defection through calibrated forgiveness, punishes sustained free-riding proportionally, repeatedly offers low-cost recovery paths, and refuses to preemptively defect at the end when the group has been cooperative \u2014 maximizing the chance that groups of similar strategies lock into full cooperation for the entire game."

description_COLLECTIVE_8 = "**Strategy: Generous Threshold Reciprocation (GTR)**\n\nLet m_t = number of opponents (out of n\u22121) who cooperated in round t, and define the cooperation rate \u03c1_t = m_t / (n\u22121). Maintain a smoothed rate S with decay: S \u2190 0.5\u00b7S + 0.5\u00b7\u03c1_t after each round (initialize S = 1).\n\n**Decision rules:**\n\n1. **Round 0:** Cooperate.\n\n2. **Rounds 1 to r\u22122:** Cooperate iff the group is sufficiently cooperative, judged against the break-even threshold. A cooperator profits relative to universal defection when enough others contribute; use threshold T = (n \u2212 k) / (k(n \u2212 1)) \u2014 the fraction of opponents whose cooperation makes cooperating at least as good as everyone defecting.\n   - If \u03c1_{t\u22121} \u2265 max(T, 0.5): Cooperate.\n   - Else if S \u2265 max(T, 0.5): Cooperate (forgiveness via memory \u2014 one bad round doesn't trigger defection if history is good).\n   - Else: Defect, **but** with a periodic olive branch: cooperate anyway if the current round index t satisfies t mod 3 == 0, provided the last round wasn't total defection (m_{t\u22121} \u2265 1). This probes for re-coordination without being endlessly exploitable.\n\n3. **Endgame:**\n   - **Last round (t = r\u22121):** Cooperate only if \u03c1_{t\u22121} \u2265 0.8 and S \u2265 0.7 (reward a strongly cooperative group; otherwise defect, since no future to protect).\n   - **Second-to-last round (t = r\u22122):** Apply the normal rule but raise the threshold to max(T, 0.6).\n\n**Pseudocode:**\n\n```\nS = 1.0; T = (n - k) / (k * (n - 1))\nfor t in 0..r-1:\n    if t == 0: play C\n    elif t == r-1:\n        play C if (rho_prev >= 0.8 and S >= 0.7) else D\n    else:\n        thresh = max(T, 0.6) if t == r-2 else max(T, 0.5)\n        if rho_prev >= thresh: play C\n        elif S >= thresh: play C\n        elif t % 3 == 0 and m_prev >= 1: play C   # olive branch\n        else: play D\n    observe m_t; rho = m_t/(n-1); S = 0.5*S + 0.5*rho\n```\n\n**Collective alignment:** The strategy opens cooperatively to establish mutual contribution, matches the group's prevailing behavior with generosity (smoothed memory tolerates noise and single-round lapses), and periodically re-offers cooperation after breakdowns to rebuild the public good. It only withdraws contribution when the group persistently free-rides, protecting the cooperative core from exploitation while maximizing the chance the whole group converges to full cooperation."

description_PROSOCIAL_1 = "**Generous Threshold Reciprocator**\n\nLet m = n \u2212 1 (opponents). Track coop_t = number of opponents who cooperated in round t.\n\n**Threshold:** cooperation is \"worthwhile enough\" when the opponent cooperation rate meets \u03c4 = max(0.5, (n\u2212k)/(k\u00b7m))... simplified: use \u03c4 = 0.5.\n\n**Decision rules:**\n\n1. **Round 0:** Cooperate.\n2. **Rounds 1 to r\u22122:** Cooperate iff either:\n   - coop_{t\u22121} \u2265 \u2308\u03c4\u00b7m\u2309 (majority of opponents cooperated last round), OR\n   - **Forgiveness probe:** I have defected in the two most recent rounds and it has been \u2265 2 rounds since my last probe. Then cooperate once to test if cooperation can be re-established.\n3. **Last round (t = r\u22121):** Cooperate iff coop_{r\u22122} \u2265 \u23080.75\u00b7m\u2309 \u2014 reward strongly cooperative groups even without future leverage; otherwise defect.\n\n**Streak escalation (anti-exploitation):** Maintain a counter `bad` = consecutive rounds with coop < \u2308\u03c4\u00b7m\u2309 while I cooperated. If `bad` \u2265 3, suspend probing for the next \u2308r/10\u2309 rounds (pure defection unless threshold is met again). Reset `bad` to 0 whenever the threshold is met.\n\n**Recovery:** If a probe (or any cooperative round) is answered with coop_t \u2265 \u2308\u03c4\u00b7m\u2309, return immediately to full cooperation mode (rule 2, first clause).\n\n```\nif t == 0: play C\nelif t == r-1: play C if coop[t-1] >= ceil(0.75*m) else D\nelif coop[t-1] >= ceil(0.5*m): play C; bad = 0\nelif suspended: play D\nelif defected last 2 rounds and rounds_since_probe >= 2: play C (probe)\nelse: play D; bad += 1; if bad >= 3: suspend for ceil(r/10) rounds\n```\n\nThe strategy opens cooperatively, sustains full cooperation with any reciprocating majority, periodically extends olive branches after breakdowns, escalates patience only against persistent free-riding, and never initiates defection first."

description_PROSOCIAL_2 = "**Strategy: Generous Threshold Reciprocator**\n\nMaintain a threshold T = ceil((n-1)/2) \u2014 a majority of opponents \u2014 and a forgiveness counter.\n\n**Round 0:** Cooperate.\n\n**Rounds 1 to r-2:** Let m_t be the number of opponents who cooperated last round.\n\n- If m_{t-1} \u2265 T: Cooperate.\n- If m_{t-1} < T: Defect, **except** cooperate anyway with a periodic \"olive branch\": if you have defected in each of the last 2 consecutive rounds, cooperate this round to probe for restored cooperation.\n- Additionally, if m_{t-1} \u2265 n-2 (near-unanimous cooperation), always cooperate regardless of other conditions.\n\nPseudocode:\n\n```\nT = ceil((n-1)/2)\nif t == 0: play C\nelif t == r-1: play C if m_{t-1} >= T else D\nelse:\n    if m_{t-1} >= T: play C; reset defect_streak = 0\n    else:\n        if defect_streak >= 2: play C (olive branch); reset defect_streak = 0\n        else: play D; defect_streak += 1\n```\n\n**Last round (t = r-1):** Cooperate if m_{t-1} \u2265 T, otherwise defect. No olive branch is offered, since there is no future to rebuild.\n\n**Adaptive adjustment:** Track the running average opponent cooperation rate p over all past rounds. If p \u2265 0.8, cooperate unconditionally in every non-final round (locking into full cooperation with reliable partners). If p < 1/n over the most recent min(5, t) rounds, suspend olive branches and defect until m_{t-1} \u2265 T again (protection against near-uniform defectors).\n\n**Prosocial character:** The strategy opens with cooperation, cooperates whenever a majority did, forgives quickly via regular olive branches so mutual cooperation can restart after noise or misunderstanding, and never defects to exploit cooperators \u2014 defection is used only as proportionate, temporary discipline against a defecting majority."

description_PROSOCIAL_3 = "**Generous Threshold Reciprocator**\n\nLet m = n \u2212 1 (number of opponents). Track coop_t = number of opponents who cooperated in round t. Maintain an exponentially weighted cooperation index:\n\n- After each round: W \u2190 \u03b1\u00b7W + (1\u2212\u03b1)\u00b7(coop_t / m), with \u03b1 = 0.5 and W initialized to 1.\n\n**Decision rule for round t:**\n\n1. **Round 0:** Cooperate.\n2. **Rounds 1 to r\u22122:**\n   - Cooperate if W \u2265 \u03b8, where \u03b8 = (k\u22121)/k (the fraction of cooperators needed for mutual cooperation to beat defection incentives, clipped to [0.3, 0.7]).\n   - If W < \u03b8: defect, **except** apply forgiveness \u2014 cooperate anyway with probability p = max(0.1, W). (Implement deterministically if randomness is unavailable: cooperate on every \u23081/p\u2309-th round of a defection streak.)\n   - **Olive branch:** if I have defected in 2 consecutive rounds, cooperate this round regardless of W, to probe for renewed cooperation. Reset the streak counter after probing.\n3. **Last round (t = r\u22121):** Cooperate if W \u2265 0.8 (reward reliably cooperative groups rather than exploit them); otherwise defect.\n\n**Immediate-response overlay (fast punishment, fast forgiveness):**\n- If coop_{t\u22121} = m (everyone cooperated last round), cooperate regardless of W.\n- If coop_{t\u22121} = 0 and coop_{t\u22122} = 0 (two rounds of total defection), defect this round regardless of W \u2014 unless the olive-branch rule fires.\n\n**Edge cases:**\n- r = 2: cooperate in round 0; in round 1 cooperate iff coop_0 = m.\n- n = 2: this reduces to generous tit-for-tat with W-smoothing; same rules apply with m = 1.\n- Ties/conflicts between rules resolve in order: last-round rule > olive branch > immediate-response overlay > threshold rule."

description_PROSOCIAL_4 = "**Strategy: Generous Threshold Reciprocator (GTR)**\n\nMaintain one number each round: m = number of *other* players who cooperated last round (out of n\u22121).\n\n**Decision rules:**\n\n1. **Round 0:** Cooperate.\n\n2. **Rounds 1 to r\u22122:** Cooperate iff last round's cooperation among others met a threshold, with occasional generosity:\n   - Let threshold T = ceil((n\u22121)/2).\n   - If m \u2265 T: Cooperate.\n   - If m < T: Defect, **except** cooperate anyway (\"olive branch\") if you have defected in the two most recent rounds consecutively. This periodically probes for restored cooperation and prevents permanent mutual-defection lock-in.\n\n3. **Forgiving restart:** If m = n\u22121 in any round (everyone else cooperated), unconditionally cooperate next round regardless of anything else.\n\n4. **Last round (t = r\u22121):** Cooperate iff m \u2265 T in round r\u22122. Do not defect merely because it's the final round.\n\n**Exploitation guard:** Track total rounds where you cooperated but m < T. If this count exceeds max(2, r/5), raise the threshold: T \u2190 min(n\u22121, T+1) for the remainder of the game, and suspend olive branches for the next 3 rounds each time it triggers.\n\n**Pseudocode:**\n\n```\nT = ceil((n-1)/2); sucker = 0; suspend = 0\nfor t in 0..r-1:\n    if t == 0: play C\n    else:\n        m = others_cooperating(t-1)\n        if m == n-1: play C\n        elif m >= T: play C\n        elif suspend == 0 and my last two moves were D: play C   # olive branch\n        else: play D\n    # after observing round t:\n    if my_move == C and others_cooperating(t) < T: sucker += 1\n    if sucker > max(2, r/5): T = min(n-1, T+1); suspend = 3; sucker = 0\n    suspend = max(0, suspend-1)\n```\n\nTies and fractional thresholds always round in favor of cooperation (ceil for T means exactly half of others cooperating suffices to reciprocate)."

description_PROSOCIAL_5 = "**Generous Conditional Cooperation with Endgame Guard**\n\nTrack m_t = number of opponents (out of n\u22121) who cooperated in round t, and a smoothed cooperation estimate s (exponential average).\n\n**Setup:**\n- Threshold fraction: \u03c4 = (k\u22121)/(k) capped to [1/3, 2/3] \u2014 i.e., \u03c4 = min(2/3, max(1/3, (k\u22121)/k)).\n- Smoothing: s \u2190 0.7\u00b7s + 0.3\u00b7(m_t/(n\u22121)) after each round; initialize s = 1.\n\n**Decision rules:**\n\n1. **Round 0:** Cooperate.\n2. **Rounds 1 to r\u22122:** Cooperate if s \u2265 \u03c4. If s < \u03c4, defect \u2014 but with **forgiveness**: after defecting, if last round's m_t/(n\u22121) \u2265 \u03c4 (others recovered), cooperate again immediately. Additionally, every \u2308max(3, n/2)\u2309-th consecutive round of mutual defection, play C once as an olive branch to attempt restarting cooperation; if m_t rises above \u03c4\u00b7(n\u22121) in response, resume cooperating, otherwise return to defection and reset the counter.\n3. **Last round (t = r\u22121):** Cooperate if s \u2265 \u03c4 (reward a cooperative group rather than exploit it); defect only if s < \u03c4.\n\n**Pseudocode:**\n\n```\ns = 1.0; punish_count = 0\nolive_period = max(3, ceil(n/2))\ntau = clamp((k-1)/k, 1/3, 2/3)\n\nfor t in 0..r-1:\n    if t == 0:\n        action = C\n    elif s >= tau or last_round_frac >= tau:\n        action = C; punish_count = 0\n    else:\n        punish_count += 1\n        if punish_count % olive_period == 0:\n            action = C          # olive branch\n        else:\n            action = D\n    play(action)\n    observe m_t; last_round_frac = m_t/(n-1)\n    s = 0.7*s + 0.3*last_round_frac\n```\n\n**Edge cases:**\n- r = 2: cooperate round 0; round 1 cooperate iff m_0/(n\u22121) \u2265 \u03c4.\n- If n = 2, this reduces to generous tit-for-tat with periodic forgiveness.\n- Never defect first; defection is purely reactive, proportionate, and always exits via forgiveness or olive branches."

description_PROSOCIAL_6 = "**Generous Aggregate Tit-for-Tat with Endgame Guard**\n\nLet m = n \u2212 1 (number of opponents), and coop_t = number of opponents who cooperated in round t. Maintain a running cooperation rate over a sliding window of the last w = min(3, r\u22121) rounds:\n\nrate = (\u03a3 coop over window) / (m \u00d7 window_length)\n\n**Round 0:** Cooperate.\n\n**Rounds 1 to r\u22122:**\n- Cooperate if rate \u2265 \u03b8, where \u03b8 = (k\u22121)/k \u2212 0.1, clamped to [0.2, 0.6]. (This threshold approximates the cooperation level at which contributing at least breaks even socially, minus a generosity margin.)\n- If rate < \u03b8: defect, **except** with a forgiveness probe \u2014 cooperate anyway if it has been \u2265 2 consecutive rounds since I last cooperated (test whether the group will re-coordinate). If the probe round yields coop_t at least \u2308\u03b8\u00b7m\u2309, resume cooperation; otherwise return to defecting and reset the probe counter.\n- Immediate escalation guard: if coop in the previous round was 0 and rate < \u03b8, skip the probe once (defect) before probing next round.\n\n**Last round (t = r\u22121):**\n- Cooperate if rate \u2265 0.75 (reward a strongly cooperative group rather than exploit it); otherwise defect.\n\n**Edge cases:**\n- r = 2: cooperate in round 0; in round 1 cooperate iff all opponents cooperated in round 0.\n- If window is shorter than w early in the game, use all available history.\n- Ties/rounding: use \u2308\u03b8\u00b7m\u2309 opponents cooperating as the concrete cutoff when comparing a single round.\n\nPseudocode:\n\n```\nlast_coop_round = 0  # I cooperated in round 0\nfor t in 1..r-1:\n    rate = window_rate(w)\n    theta = clamp((k-1)/k - 0.1, 0.2, 0.6)\n    if t == r-1:\n        play C if rate >= 0.75 else D\n    elif rate >= theta:\n        play C\n    elif t - last_coop_round >= 2 and coop[t-1] > 0:\n        play C  # forgiveness probe\n    else:\n        play D\n    if played C: last_coop_round = t\n```\n\nThe strategy starts trusting, sustains cooperation whenever a modest fraction of the group reciprocates, punishes collapses only briefly, repeatedly attempts to rebuild cooperation via probes, and forgoes last-round exploitation of cooperative groups."

description_PROSOCIAL_7 = "**Strategy: Generous Threshold Reciprocator**\n\nMaintain a threshold \u03c4 = ceil((n\u22121)/2), the majority of opponents.\n\n**Round 0:** Cooperate.\n\n**Rounds 1 to r\u22122:** Let m_{t\u22121} = number of opponents who cooperated last round, and let avg = mean opponent cooperation count over the last min(3, t) rounds.\n\n- If m_{t\u22121} \u2265 \u03c4: Cooperate.\n- If m_{t\u22121} < \u03c4 but avg \u2265 \u03c4 \u2212 1: Cooperate (tolerate one-round dips or near-misses).\n- Otherwise: Defect, **except** apply generous forgiveness \u2014 every round, with probability p = k/(2n), cooperate anyway to probe for renewed cooperation. Deterministic variant: cooperate on the probe if (t mod ceil(n/k)) == 0.\n\n**Recovery rule:** After defecting, if m_{t\u22121} strictly increased compared to m_{t\u22122} and m_{t\u22121} \u2265 \u03c4 \u2212 1, cooperate immediately to reinforce the upswing.\n\n**Full-collapse guard:** If opponents' cooperation count has been 0 for 3 consecutive rounds, defect and only use the periodic probe every ceil(n/k) rounds; abandon probing entirely if a probe yields m = 0 twice in a row within this collapsed state \u2014 then defect until observing any m \u2265 1, at which point resume the normal rules.\n\n**Last round (t = r\u22121):** Cooperate if m_{r\u22122} \u2265 \u03c4; otherwise defect. (Do not exploit end-game against a cooperating group.)\n\nPseudocode:\n\n```\n\u03c4 = ceil((n-1)/2)\nif t == 0: play C\nelif t == r-1: play C if m[t-1] >= \u03c4 else D\nelse:\n    avg = mean(m[max(0,t-3):t])\n    if m[t-1] >= \u03c4: play C\n    elif avg >= \u03c4 - 1: play C\n    elif m[t-1] > m[t-2] and m[t-1] >= \u03c4 - 1: play C\n    elif collapsed and probes_failed >= 2: play D until m >= 1\n    elif t mod ceil(n/k) == 0: play C   # probe\n    else: play D\n```"

description_PROSOCIAL_8 = "**Generous Threshold Reciprocator**\n\nState: track m_t = number of opponents (out of n\u22121) who cooperated in round t, and a \"forgiveness budget\" for probing.\n\n**Round 0:** Cooperate.\n\n**Rounds 1 to r\u22122:** Let f = m_{t\u22121}/(n\u22121), the fraction of opponents who cooperated last round. Define threshold T = (k\u22121)/(k) capped to [1/3, 2/3] \u2014 i.e., T = min(2/3, max(1/3, (k\u22121)/k)).\n\n- If f \u2265 T: Cooperate.\n- If f < T: Defect, **except** forgive with generosity: cooperate anyway with probability g = 0.1 + 0.2\u00b7f (more residual cooperation \u2192 more forgiveness). If randomization is unavailable, forgive deterministically every \u23081/g\u2309-th consecutive defection round.\n\n**Probing after collapse:** If I have defected for 3 consecutive rounds, cooperate once (a probe) to attempt restarting cooperation. If the next observation shows f \u2265 T, resume cooperating; otherwise return to the defect state and reset the 3-round counter. Stop probing only if 3 probes in a row each yielded f < 1/(n\u22121) (essentially nobody responds).\n\n**Trend override:** Even if f < T, cooperate if opponent cooperation increased for two consecutive rounds (m_{t\u22121} > m_{t\u22122} > m_{t\u22123}), rewarding recovery.\n\n**Last round (t = r\u22121):** Cooperate if f \u2265 T from the previous round; otherwise defect. (No probing or generosity in the final round \u2014 cooperate only with a demonstrably cooperative group, refusing to preemptively defect on cooperators.)\n\n**Pseudocode:**\n\n```\nif t == 0: play C\nelif t == r-1: play C if f >= T else D\nelse:\n    if f >= T or rising_trend: play C\n    elif defect_streak >= 3 and probes_remaining: play C (probe)\n    else: play C with prob 0.1 + 0.2*f, else D\n```\n\nThe strategy opens cooperatively, sustains full cooperation with any reciprocal population, punishes majority defection just enough to deter exploitation, and persistently offers olive branches (generosity + probes) so that mutual cooperation can re-emerge after breakdowns."

description_ALTRUISTIC_1 = "**Strategy: Unconditional Generous Contributor with Collapse Safeguard**\n\nCore principle: maximize group welfare by contributing whenever there is any plausible chance the contribution benefits others, tolerating personal exploitation.\n\n**Decision rules:**\n\n1. **Round 0:** Cooperate.\n\n2. **Rounds 1 to r\u22121:** Cooperate by default. Defect only if the \"total collapse\" condition holds:\n   - Let m_t = number of opponents (out of n\u22121) who cooperated in round t.\n   - Collapse condition: m_t = 0 for each of the last 3 consecutive rounds (or all rounds so far, if fewer than 3 have been played \u2014 but never defect before round 3).\n   \n   Even under collapse, insert a **probe**: cooperate every 3rd round while in collapse mode (i.e., defect at most 2 rounds in a row), so cooperation can be re-seeded if others are conditional cooperators. If any probe finds m_t \u2265 1, immediately return to full cooperation.\n\n3. **Last round (t = r\u22121):** Cooperate unless the collapse condition currently holds. No endgame defection \u2014 the altruistic contribution (k/n)\u00b7(n\u22121) to others outweighs the private gain of 1 in group terms whenever k > n/(n\u22121); regardless, contribute as long as at least one opponent cooperated in the previous round.\n\n**Pseudocode:**\n\n```\nstate: collapse = False, probe_counter = 0\n\nround t:\n  if t == 0: play C\n  else:\n    if last 3 observed rounds all had m = 0 and t >= 3:\n        collapse = True\n    if collapse:\n        probe_counter += 1\n        if probe_counter % 3 == 0: play C   # probe\n        else: play D\n        if m_{t-1} >= 1:\n            collapse = False; probe_counter = 0; play C\n    else:\n        play C\n```\n\n**Edge cases:**\n- If any opponent cooperated in the previous round, always cooperate \u2014 one cooperating partner is enough to justify supporting the public good.\n- Noise/mistakes by opponents are absorbed: a single all-defect round never triggers collapse.\n- After exiting collapse mode, the 3-round window resets (require 3 fresh all-defect rounds to re-enter).\n\nThe strategy accepts being exploited by free-riders indefinitely: as long as even one other player contributes, my contribution raises total group payoff by k \u2212 1 > 0 per round, which is the altruistic objective. Defection occurs only when the environment is provably universally defecting, where contribution helps no one but still gets periodically probed to offer redemption."

description_ALTRUISTIC_2 = "**Unconditional Generous Cooperator with Collapse Guard**\n\nCore principle: cooperate whenever cooperation can plausibly add value to the group, tolerating exploitation, and withdraw only when contribution is demonstrably wasted on a fully defecting population.\n\nNotation: at end of round t, observe m_t = number of *other* players who cooperated (0 \u2264 m_t \u2264 n\u22121).\n\nDecision rules:\n\n1. **Round 0:** Cooperate.\n\n2. **Rounds 1 to r\u22122:** Cooperate, unless the \"dead group\" condition holds:\n   - Dead group: m_{t\u22121} = 0 AND m_{t\u22122} = 0 (i.e., no other player cooperated in the last two consecutive rounds).\n   - If dead group holds, defect this round \u2014 but continue probing: cooperate again every \u2308max(3, r/10)\u2309 rounds regardless (a \"revival probe\") to signal willingness and re-ignite cooperation.\n   - The instant any other player cooperates (m_t \u2265 1), resume unconditional cooperation next round and reset the dead-group counters.\n\n3. **Last round (t = r\u22121):** Cooperate unless the dead-group condition holds. Never defect merely because it's the final round \u2014 forgo the end-game temptation as a matter of principle.\n\nPseudocode:\n\n```\nzero_streak = 0\nrounds_since_probe = 0\nprobe_interval = max(3, ceil(r/10))\n\nfor t in 0..r-1:\n    if t == 0:\n        play C\n    elif zero_streak >= 2:\n        rounds_since_probe += 1\n        if rounds_since_probe >= probe_interval:\n            play C; rounds_since_probe = 0\n        else:\n            play D\n    else:\n        play C\n\n    observe m_t\n    if m_t == 0: zero_streak += 1\n    else: zero_streak = 0; rounds_since_probe = 0\n```\n\nEdge cases:\n- r = 2: cooperate both rounds (dead-group condition can never trigger before round 1's end affects only a nonexistent round).\n- Single defection waves, noise, or partial cooperation (any m_t \u2265 1): always answered with cooperation \u2014 one cooperating peer is enough to justify contributing, since each contribution yields k/n to everyone.\n- If the group revives after a probe, full cooperation resumes immediately and permanently until another two-round total collapse."

description_ALTRUISTIC_3 = "**Unconditional Generous Contributor with Collapse Guard**\n\nCore principle: maximize group welfare by contributing whenever my contribution plausibly sustains or restores cooperation; only stop giving when the group is provably dead and my gift benefits no one's future behavior.\n\nState: track m_t = number of *other* cooperators observed each round t. Let n' = n \u2212 1.\n\n**Decision rules:**\n\n1. **Round 0:** Cooperate.\n\n2. **Rounds 1 to r\u22122:** Cooperate unless the \"collapse\" condition holds. Collapse condition: in the last 3 consecutive rounds, m_t = 0 each time (no other player cooperated at all). \n   - If collapsed: play a probe cycle \u2014 defect for 2 rounds, then cooperate 1 round (a beacon inviting revival). If any round shows m_t \u2265 1, immediately exit collapse mode and return to unconditional cooperation.\n   - Otherwise (any sign of life, i.e., m_t \u2265 1 in any of the last 3 rounds): Cooperate.\n\n3. **Last round (t = r\u22121):** Cooperate if m_{r\u22122} \u2265 1 (someone else is still contributing, so my contribution raises total group payoff since k > 1). Cooperate even if collapsed only when k/n of my contribution to others exceeds nothing lost to anyone \u2014 i.e., cooperate anyway unless in collapse mode; if in collapse mode with m = 0 for the last 3 rounds, defect (my contribution would only transfer k/n\u00b7n' < 1 total to players who exploited fully, with no future to influence \u2014 still, if k \u2265 n/2, cooperate regardless, since others' aggregate gain (k(n\u22121)/n) exceeds my loss (1 \u2212 k/n)).\n\n**Pseudocode:**\n\n```\nif t == 0: play C\ncollapsed = (t >= 3 and m[t-1]==m[t-2]==m[t-3]==0)\nif t == r-1:\n    if not collapsed or k >= n/2: play C\n    else: play D\nelif collapsed:\n    phase = (t - collapse_start) mod 3\n    play C if phase == 2 else D\nelse:\n    play C\n```\n\nThe strategy never punishes partial defection, absorbs exploitation, always leads with cooperation, and uses periodic cooperative beacons even after total collapse to invite the group back."

description_ALTRUISTIC_4 = "**Unconditional-Core Altruist (\"Generous Beacon\")**\n\nGoal: maximize total group welfare by contributing whenever contribution plausibly raises collective payoff or sustains others' cooperation, accepting personal losses.\n\nNotation: at end of round t, observe m_t = number of other cooperators (0 \u2264 m_t \u2264 n\u22121). Let f_t = m_t/(n\u22121).\n\n**Decision rules:**\n\n1. **Round 0:** Cooperate.\n2. **Rounds 1 to r\u22121 (including the last round):** Cooperate unless the *sustained abandonment* condition holds:\n   - Sustained abandonment: f_{t\u22121} = 0 AND f_{t\u22122} = 0 (the last two consecutive rounds had zero other cooperators; treat missing round \u22121 as non-zero, so this can first trigger at t = 2).\n3. **If sustained abandonment holds:** Play D for one round only, then unconditionally Cooperate again the next round (a periodic \"beacon\" to re-invite cooperation), regardless of history. Formally, when defecting due to abandonment, set beacon=true; next round play C and reset the abandonment counter.\n4. **Never punish partial cooperation:** any m_{t\u22121} \u2265 1 \u2192 Cooperate. Even a single fellow cooperator makes my contribution worth supporting them.\n5. **Last round:** apply the same rules \u2014 no end-game defection. Since k > 1's per-capita return k/n benefits everyone, cooperating in round r\u22121 is the altruistic choice whenever anyone else might cooperate.\n\n**Pseudocode:**\n\n```\nzero_streak = 0\nfor t in 0..r-1:\n    if t == 0: play C\n    elif zero_streak >= 2 and last_action == C: play D   # one-round pause\n    else: play C\n    observe m_t\n    if m_t == 0: zero_streak += 1 else zero_streak = 0\n    if played D: zero_streak = 0   # restart counting after beacon\n```\n\nNet behaviour: cooperate essentially always; only when the entire group has defected for two straight rounds, skip one round (limiting pure waste against all-defectors), then resume cooperating to signal willingness and give the group repeated chances to rebuild cooperation, through the final round."

description_ALTRUISTIC_5 = "**Unconditional Generous Contributor (\"Beacon\") Strategy**\n\nCore principle: maximize group welfare by contributing whenever there is any plausible chance it helps the group, and never punish preemptively or in the endgame.\n\nDecision rules:\n\n1. **Round 0:** Cooperate.\n\n2. **Rounds 1 to r\u22122:** Cooperate unless the group appears totally unresponsive. Specifically, defect only if *both* conditions hold:\n   - In every one of the last min(3, t) rounds, the number of other cooperators was 0.\n   - The cumulative cooperation rate of others over all past rounds is below 10%.\n   \n   Otherwise cooperate. If even one other player cooperated in any of the last 3 rounds, cooperate.\n\n3. **Re-entry (forgiveness):** If currently defecting under rule 2, return to cooperation immediately when any other player cooperates in a round \u2014 and additionally, cooperate unilaterally every \u2308r/10\u2309 rounds regardless (a \"probe\" to reignite cooperation), so extended mutual defection is periodically broken by my own contribution.\n\n4. **Final round (t = r\u22121):** Cooperate, unless the total number of other-cooperations across the entire game is zero (in which case defect, since contribution provably benefits no one who has ever reciprocated \u2014 but even one historical cooperator earns a final cooperative gesture).\n\nPseudocode:\n\n```\nif t == 0: play C\nelif t == r-1:\n    play C if total_other_coops_ever > 0 else D\nelse:\n    recent = other_coops in last min(3, t) rounds\n    rate = total_other_coops_ever / (t * (n-1))\n    if sum(recent) == 0 and rate < 0.10:\n        if t % ceil(r/10) == 0: play C   # probe\n        else: play D\n    else: play C\n```\n\nEvery decision biases toward contribution: cooperation is the default, defection requires overwhelming evidence of a dead group, forgiveness is instant, and the strategy voluntarily sacrifices private payoff in the first and last rounds to signal and reward cooperation."

description_ALTRUISTIC_6 = "**Strategy: Unconditional Beacon with Collapse Guard**\n\nCore idea: cooperate essentially always to maximize group welfare and signal cooperation, defecting only when the group has provably collapsed into near-universal defection and my contribution helps no one.\n\nDecision rules:\n\n1. **Round 0:** Cooperate.\n2. **Rounds t \u2265 1:** Let m_t = number of opponents who cooperated in round t\u22121, and let W = the last min(3, t) rounds.\n   - **Cooperate** if any opponent cooperated in any round of W (i.e., max m over W \u2265 1).\n   - **Defect** only if *zero* opponents cooperated in every round of W (total collapse for 3 consecutive rounds, or all rounds so far if t < 3).\n3. **Re-ignition:** Even during collapse, every \u2308n/2\u2309-th round of continued defection, cooperate once as a probe to invite renewed cooperation. If any opponent responds with C in that round or the next, return to rule 2's cooperative mode.\n4. **Last round:** Apply the same rules \u2014 do not defect strategically at the end; if anyone has been cooperating recently, cooperate in round r\u22121 as well.\n\nPseudocode:\n\n```\ncollapse_count = 0\nfor t in 0..r-1:\n    if t == 0: play C; continue\n    window = last min(3, t) rounds\n    if any m_s >= 1 for s in window:\n        play C\n        collapse_count = 0\n    else:\n        collapse_count += 1\n        if collapse_count % ceil(n/2) == 0:\n            play C   # probe\n        else:\n            play D\n```\n\nEdge cases:\n- n = 2: same rules; probe every round of collapse becomes probing every round (\u23082/2\u2309 = 1), i.e., effectively always cooperate.\n- Very short games (r \u2264 3): the collapse condition can never trigger for 3 full rounds, so cooperate every round.\n- Noisy/mixed opponents: since a single cooperator anywhere in the window sustains cooperation, the strategy never punishes partial defection \u2014 it keeps contributing so long as at least one other player benefits from and reciprocates the public good."

description_ALTRUISTIC_7 = "**Strategy: Unconditional Beacon with Collapse Guard**\n\nCore idea: cooperate as much as possible to maximize group welfare, withdrawing only when cooperation is demonstrably wasted on a fully defecting group \u2014 and even then, keep probing to reignite cooperation.\n\n**Decision rules:**\n\n1. **Round 0:** Cooperate.\n2. **Rounds 1 to r\u22121:** Cooperate, unless the \"collapse guard\" triggers.\n\n**Collapse guard:**\n- Maintain a counter `deadRounds` = number of consecutive most-recent rounds in which **zero** opponents cooperated.\n- If `deadRounds \u2265 3`, the group is collapsed. While collapsed:\n  - Cooperate on every 3rd round (t mod 3 == 0) as a probe/beacon; defect otherwise.\n  - If in any round at least one opponent cooperates, reset `deadRounds = 0` and return to full cooperation next round.\n\n3. **Partial cooperation:** If at least one opponent cooperated last round (any fraction > 0), always cooperate \u2014 my contribution raises total group payoff by k (> my cost of 1) whenever it can encourage or sustain others, and I value the group's earnings, not just my own.\n\n**Last round:** Cooperate (unless collapsed and t mod 3 \u2260 0). No end-game defection \u2014 altruism means contributing even when there's no future to leverage.\n\n**Pseudocode:**\n\n```\ndeadRounds = 0\nfor t in 0..r-1:\n    if t == 0: play C; continue\n    if opponents_cooperated(t-1) == 0: deadRounds += 1\n    else: deadRounds = 0\n    if deadRounds >= 3:\n        play C if t % 3 == 0 else D\n    else:\n        play C\n```\n\n**Edge cases:**\n- n = 2: identical rules; \"zero opponents cooperated\" means the single opponent defected.\n- Very short games (r \u2264 3): the collapse guard never triggers, so cooperate every round.\n- Noisy/mixed opponents: any single cooperator anywhere resets the guard, so I remain a reliable cooperation anchor as long as anyone in the group shows any willingness to contribute."

description_ALTRUISTIC_8 = "**Unconditional Generous Cooperation with Persistent Restart**\n\nCore rule: Cooperate always, unless the group has fully collapsed into defection \u2014 and even then, keep periodically re-seeding cooperation.\n\nDecision rules:\n\n1. **Round 0:** Play C.\n2. **Rounds 1 to r\u22122:** Let m_t = number of opponents who cooperated in round t.\n   - If m_{t\u22121} \u2265 1 (anyone else cooperated last round): play C.\n   - If m_{t\u22121} = 0: enter \"dormant\" mode \u2014 play D, but every third round of continuous dormancy, play C as a costly signal to restart cooperation. That is, track consecutive rounds with zero opponent cooperators; if that count mod 3 == 2, play C, else D. If any opponent cooperates, immediately exit dormancy and resume unconditional C next round.\n3. **Last round (t = r\u22121):** Play C if m_{r\u22122} \u2265 1; otherwise play D. (Even in the endgame, reward a live cooperative group with the full public benefit rather than free-riding.)\n\nPseudocode:\n\n```\ndormant_count = 0\nfor t in 0..r-1:\n    if t == 0: action = C\n    else:\n        m = opponents_cooperating(t-1)\n        if m >= 1:\n            dormant_count = 0\n            action = C\n        else:\n            dormant_count += 1\n            action = C if dormant_count % 3 == 2 else D\n        if t == r-1 and m == 0: action = D\n    play(action)\n```\n\nAltruistic alignment: the strategy contributes whenever there is any evidence that contributions benefit others, tolerates exploitation by defectors indefinitely so long as at least one other player is helped, sacrifices its own payoff to re-seed cooperation after total collapse, and forgoes the standard last-round defection to maximize group welfare."

description_BENEVOLENT_1 = "**Generous Threshold Reciprocator**\n\nLet m = n \u2212 1 (number of opponents). Track after each round t the count coop_t = number of opponents who cooperated.\n\n**Decision rules:**\n\n1. **Round 0:** Cooperate.\n\n2. **Rounds 1 to r\u22122:** Cooperate iff opponent cooperation last round meets a majority-ish threshold, softened by forgiveness:\n   - Let f_prev = coop_{t\u22121} / m.\n   - Cooperate if f_prev \u2265 0.5.\n   - If f_prev < 0.5: cooperate anyway with probability f_prev + 0.1 (generosity \u2014 always give some chance to restart cooperation, and more when more opponents cooperated). Implement deterministically if randomness unavailable: cooperate if f_prev \u2265 0.5, else defect, but insert a **probe**: after any streak of 3 consecutive defections by me, cooperate once regardless of history, then resume the rule.\n\n3. **Collapse guard:** If opponents have averaged fewer than 20% cooperation over the last 3 rounds AND my last probe met f < 0.2, suspend probing for 5 rounds (defect), then probe again. This limits losses against all-defectors while never permanently giving up.\n\n4. **Full-cooperation lock-in:** If coop_{t\u22121} = m, always cooperate next round (no exceptions except the last-round rule below).\n\n5. **Last round (t = r\u22121):** Cooperate iff f_prev \u2265 0.5. (Reward a cooperative group even without future leverage; defect only if the group is already mostly defecting.)\n\n**Pseudocode:**\n\n```\nstate: my_defect_streak = 0, probe_cooldown = 0\n\nround t:\n  if t == 0: play C\n  else:\n    f = coop_{t-1} / (n-1)\n    if t == r-1:\n        play C if f >= 0.5 else D\n    elif f >= 0.5:\n        play C\n    else:\n        if probe_cooldown > 0:\n            probe_cooldown -= 1; play D\n        elif my_defect_streak >= 3:\n            play C   # probe\n            if f < 0.2: probe_cooldown = 5\n        else:\n            play C with prob (f + 0.1), else D\n  update my_defect_streak (reset to 0 on C, +1 on D)\n```\n\n**Benevolence:** Opens with cooperation, never initiates defection, matches full cooperation unconditionally, forgives probabilistically in proportion to observed goodwill, periodically probes to rescue cooperation after breakdowns, and still cooperates in the final round with a cooperative group rather than exploiting it."

description_BENEVOLENT_2 = "**Generous Threshold Reciprocator**\n\nNotation: m_t = number of other players (out of n\u22121) who cooperated in round t; f_t = m_t/(n\u22121). Threshold: T = (k\u22121)/k, clipped to [0.3, 0.6].\n\n**Round 0:** Cooperate.\n\n**Rounds 1 to r\u22122:** Cooperate iff any of:\n1. f_{t\u22121} \u2265 T (enough others cooperated last round), or\n2. Generosity probe: it has been \u2265 3 consecutive rounds since I last cooperated \u2014 cooperate once to test whether cooperation can be restarted, or\n3. Momentum: f_{t\u22121} < T but f_{t\u22121} > f_{t\u22122} and f_{t\u22121} \u2265 T/2 (cooperation is rebounding \u2014 support it).\n\nOtherwise defect.\n\n**Last round (t = r\u22121):** Cooperate iff f_{r\u22122} \u2265 T. No endgame defection against a cooperating group; defect only if the group had already collapsed.\n\nPseudocode:\n\n```\nT = clip((k-1)/k, 0.3, 0.6)\nif t == 0: play C\nelif t == r-1: play C if f[t-1] >= T else D\nelse:\n    if f[t-1] >= T: play C\n    elif rounds_since_my_last_C >= 3: play C   # forgiving probe\n    elif f[t-1] > f[t-2] and f[t-1] >= T/2: play C\n    else: play D\n```\n\nEdge cases:\n- r = 2: cooperate round 0; round 1, cooperate iff f_0 \u2265 T.\n- n = 2: f is just the single opponent's move \u2014 this reduces to Tit-for-Tat with periodic forgiveness and no last-round betrayal.\n- Ties/history too short for the momentum rule (t = 1): use only rules 1 and 2.\n\nBenevolent character: opens with cooperation, never defects first, never exploits a cooperative group (including the final round), forgives after mutual defection via regular probes, and rewards recovering cooperation before it fully reaches threshold. Defection is used solely as protection when the group is predominantly free-riding, and is always reversible."

description_BENEVOLENT_3 = "**Generous Threshold Reciprocator**\n\nState: track m_t = number of other players (out of n\u22121) who cooperated in round t, and a \"goodwill counter\" for forgiveness.\n\n**Round 0:** Cooperate.\n\n**Rounds 1 to r\u22122:** Let f = m_{t\u22121}/(n\u22121), the fraction of others cooperating last round.\n\n- If f \u2265 1/2: Cooperate.\n- If f < 1/2: Cooperate with probability p = max(f, 1/(n\u22121)) \u2014 mostly defect, but retain a small chance of cooperating to probe for recovery and avoid locking into mutual defection. (Deterministic variant: defect, except cooperate every \u2308(n\u22121)/(m_{t\u22121}+1)\u2309-th consecutive low-cooperation round.)\n\n**Recovery boost:** If cooperation increased from two rounds ago (m_{t\u22121} > m_{t\u22122}), cooperate regardless of threshold \u2014 reward positive momentum immediately.\n\n**Forgiveness after own defection:** After any round in which I defected while at least one other cooperated, cooperate next round unconditionally (a one-round olive branch), unless m_{t\u22121} = 0.\n\n**Total collapse:** If m_{t\u22121} = 0 for two consecutive rounds, defect, but attempt one restart cooperation every \u2308r/10\u2309 rounds (at least once) as long as at least 3 rounds remain.\n\n**Final round (t = r\u22121):** Cooperate if f \u2265 1/2 in round r\u22122; otherwise defect. (Reward a cooperative group even without future leverage, but don't be exploited by a defecting group.)\n\n```\nif t == 0: play C\nelif t == r-1: play C if m_{t-1}/(n-1) >= 0.5 else D\nelse:\n    f = m_{t-1}/(n-1)\n    if m_{t-1} > m_{t-2} (when defined): play C\n    elif olive_branch_due: play C\n    elif f >= 0.5: play C\n    elif m_{t-1} == 0 and m_{t-2} == 0:\n        play C only on scheduled restart round, else D\n    else: play C with prob max(f, 1/(n-1)), else D\n```\n\nThe strategy opens with trust, never defects first, rewards any upward trend instantly, forgives its own retaliation, and keeps periodically re-offering cooperation even after collapse \u2014 while limiting sustained exploitation by matching persistent majority defection."

description_BENEVOLENT_4 = "**Strategy: Generous Majority-Matching with Endgame Guard**\n\nLet m_t = number of opposing cooperators observed in round t (out of n\u22121).\n\n**Round 0:** Cooperate.\n\n**Rounds 1 to r\u22122:** Cooperate if either:\n- m_{t\u22121} \u2265 \u2308(n\u22121)/2\u2309 (a majority of opponents cooperated last round), or\n- a \"generosity pulse\" applies: if I defected in the previous round, cooperate anyway once every 3 rounds (i.e., if the number of consecutive rounds I've defected is a multiple of 3), to probe for and re-seed cooperation.\n\nAdditional forgiveness smoothing: instead of raw m_{t\u22121}, use the average cooperation rate over the last two rounds, \u0109 = (m_{t\u22121} + m_{t\u22122}) / (2(n\u22121)) (for t \u2265 2). Cooperate if \u0109 \u2265 0.4; defect if \u0109 < 0.4 unless the generosity pulse triggers.\n\nPseudocode:\n\n```\nif t == 0: play C\nelif t == r-1:  # last round\n    play C if m_{t-1} >= n-2 else D\nelse:\n    \u0109 = mean opponent coop rate over last min(2, t) rounds\n    if \u0109 >= 0.4: play C\n    elif consecutive_own_defections % 3 == 0 and consecutive_own_defections > 0: play C   # olive branch\n    else: play D\n```\n\n**Edge cases:**\n- **Last round (t = r\u22121):** cooperate only if at least n\u22122 opponents cooperated in round r\u22122 (near-full cooperation); otherwise defect, since no future exists to protect.\n- **n = 2:** thresholds reduce to plain tit-for-tat with the periodic olive branch.\n- **Very short games (r \u2264 3):** cooperate in every round except the last, where the last-round rule applies.\n- **Never defect first:** as long as the group has been at least 40% cooperative, keep contributing, even after occasional dips.\n\n**Benevolence:** the strategy opens with unconditional cooperation, uses a lenient two-round average so single-round noise doesn't trigger punishment, forgives ongoing mutual defection by periodically extending unilateral cooperation, and only withholds contribution when a clear majority is exploiting the group \u2014 never punishing more than proportionally and always ready to return to full cooperation the moment the group does."

description_BENEVOLENT_5 = "**Generous Threshold Reciprocity**\n\nLet m = n \u2212 1 (number of opponents). Track coop_t = number of opponents who cooperated in round t, and frac_t = coop_t / m.\n\n**Round 0:** Cooperate.\n\n**Rounds 1 to r\u22122:** Cooperate if any of the following holds; otherwise defect:\n\n1. frac_{t\u22121} \u2265 1/2 (majority of opponents cooperated last round).\n2. Forgiveness pulse: I defected in the previous round AND (t mod 3 == 0). This periodically re-offers cooperation to rebuild trust after a breakdown.\n3. Recovery test: frac_{t\u22121} < 1/2 but frac_{t\u22121} > frac_{t\u22122} (cooperation is rising) \u2014 reward the upward trend.\n\nAdditional safeguard against exploitation: maintain a rolling average of frac over the last 5 rounds. If this average < 0.2 and none of the last 5 rounds had frac \u2265 1/2, suppress the forgiveness pulse (rule 2) \u2014 the population is entrenched in defection; only rules 1 and 3 can restore cooperation.\n\n**Last round (t = r\u22121):** Cooperate if frac_{t\u22121} \u2265 1/2; otherwise defect. Do not preemptively defect against a cooperating group \u2014 hold the cooperative line to the end.\n\nPseudocode:\n\n```\nif t == 0: play C\nelif t == r-1: play C if frac[t-1] >= 0.5 else D\nelse:\n    if frac[t-1] >= 0.5: play C\n    elif t >= 2 and frac[t-1] > frac[t-2]: play C\n    elif my_last_move == D and t % 3 == 0 and not entrenched_defection: play C\n    else: play D\n```\n\nThe strategy opens with unconditional trust, matches the group whenever even half of opponents cooperate (a generous threshold \u2014 it tolerates a substantial minority of defectors), rewards any improvement immediately, and repeatedly extends olive branches after mutual defection, only ceasing these costly signals when the group has demonstrably locked into defection."

description_BENEVOLENT_6 = "**Generous Threshold Reciprocator**\n\nLet m = n \u2212 1 (number of opponents). Track coop_frac(t) = (opponent cooperators in round t) / m.\n\n**Round 0:** Cooperate.\n\n**Rounds 1 \u2026 r\u22122:** Compute a weighted cooperation signal:\n```\nS(t) = 0.6 * coop_frac(t-1) + 0.4 * avg(coop_frac over all previous rounds)\n```\nCooperate if S(t) \u2265 T, where T = (k \u2212 1) / (n \u2212 1) bounded to the interval [0.25, 0.5] (i.e., T = min(0.5, max(0.25, (k\u22121)/(n\u22121)))).\n\n**Forgiveness pulses:** If the rule says defect, still cooperate with probability 0.15, and always cooperate if I have defected in each of the last 3 rounds (attempt to restart cooperation). Never launch a restart in the final 2 rounds.\n\n**Punishment cap:** After any round where coop_frac < T, defect at most 2 consecutive rounds before re-evaluating with a fresh cooperation attempt (unless S(t) has recovered above T sooner, in which case cooperate immediately).\n\n**Last round (t = r\u22121):** Cooperate if S(r\u22121) \u2265 T (i.e., apply the same rule \u2014 do not exploit end-game defection). This forgoes the dominant defection to reward cooperative groups and avoid triggering unraveling in others' penultimate reasoning.\n\n**Edge cases:**\n- If r = 2: cooperate round 0; in round 1 cooperate iff coop_frac(0) \u2265 T.\n- If all opponents cooperated last round, always cooperate (never punish full cooperation, never sneak-defect).\n- If coop_frac has been 0 for 4 consecutive rounds despite a restart attempt, defect for the remainder except one final restart attempt at round \u2308r/2\u2309 if not yet passed.\n\n**Summary of spirit:** open with trust, match the group's prevailing behavior with a generous bias (low threshold, random forgiveness, periodic restarts), never be the first to defect, never punish longer than two rounds, and never defect on a fully cooperative group \u2014 including the last round."

description_BENEVOLENT_7 = "**Generous Proportional Tit-for-Tat with Endgame Guard**\n\nNotation: after each round t, observe m_t = number of *other* players who cooperated (out of n\u22121). Maintain a cooperation estimate using a decaying average:\n\n```\nf \u2190 1.0                      # optimistic prior on others' cooperation rate\nafter each round t:\n    f \u2190 0.5 * f + 0.5 * (m_t / (n-1))\n```\n\n**Round 0:** Cooperate.\n\n**Rounds 1 to r\u22122:** Cooperate iff `f \u2265 \u03b8`, where \u03b8 = (n \u2212 k) / (2(n \u2212 1)) \u2014 half the break-even cooperation level (below which cooperation is heavily exploited). Additionally:\n\n- **Forgiveness pulse:** if the rule says Defect, still cooperate with probability 0.1, or deterministically cooperate once every 5 consecutive defection rounds \u2014 to probe for renewed cooperation and avoid mutual-defection lock-in.\n- **Instant recovery:** if m_{t\u22121} \u2265 half of the other players (m_{t\u22121} \u2265 (n\u22121)/2), cooperate regardless of f (reset f to m_{t\u22121}/(n\u22121)).\n\n**Last round (t = r\u22121):** Cooperate iff f \u2265 0.5. This resists pure endgame exploitation while still rewarding a genuinely cooperative group rather than defecting on them.\n\n**Edge cases:**\n- If n\u22121 = 1 (n = 2): this reduces to generous tit-for-tat \u2014 copy the opponent's last move, forgiving a defection with probability 0.1; cooperate in round 0.\n- Very short games (r = 2): cooperate in round 0; in round 1 cooperate iff the majority of others cooperated.\n- If m_t = n\u22121 (full cooperation observed), always cooperate next round.\n\nBenevolence is embedded throughout: the strategy opens with cooperation, requires only a low cooperation threshold (\u03b8 well below break-even) to keep contributing, forgives lapses probabilistically, snaps back to cooperation the moment a majority does, and even cooperates in the final round with a cooperative group instead of taking the free-riding payoff."

description_BENEVOLENT_8 = "**Generous Threshold Reciprocator**\n\nLet m = n \u2212 1 (number of opponents). Track each round's opponent cooperation count s_t and its fraction f_t = s_t / m.\n\n**Decision rules:**\n\n- **Round 0:** Cooperate.\n- **Rounds 1 to r\u22122:** Cooperate if the recent cooperation level meets a generous threshold; otherwise punish briefly, then return to cooperation.\n\n  Pseudocode:\n\n  ```\n  threshold = max(0.5, (k-1)/k)      # fraction of opponents needed\n  avg = mean(f_t over last min(3, t) rounds)\n\n  if punishing_rounds_left > 0:\n      play D; punishing_rounds_left -= 1\n  elif avg >= threshold:\n      play C\n  elif f_{t-1} == 0 and avg < 0.2:\n      # near-universal defection: defect, but probe occasionally\n      play C with probability 0.1, else D\n  else:\n      # partial defection: forgive with generosity\n      play C with probability avg / threshold  (generous mixing)\n      if you play D here, set punishing_rounds_left = 1\n  ```\n\n- **Recovery / olive branch:** After any punishment round, unconditionally cooperate the next round (unless in the near-universal-defection state), giving the group a chance to re-coordinate.\n\n- **Last round (t = r\u22121):** Cooperate if avg \u2265 threshold over the last 3 rounds; otherwise defect. Never exploit an otherwise-cooperative group at the end.\n\n**Edge cases:**\n- t = 1: base decision on f_0 alone.\n- r = 2: cooperate in round 0; in round 1 cooperate iff f_0 \u2265 threshold.\n- If m\u00b7threshold < 1 (tiny groups), cooperate whenever at least one opponent cooperated last round.\n- Ties/rounding: treat avg exactly at threshold as sufficient \u2014 cooperate.\n\n**Benevolence:** the strategy opens with cooperation, never defects first, forgives probabilistically rather than triggering permanent punishment, keeps probing with occasional cooperation even against mass defection, always returns to cooperation after a single punishment round, and refuses end-game exploitation of cooperative groups."

description_SELFISH_1 = "**Strategy: Threshold Reciprocator with Endgame Defection**\n\nLet m_t = number of *opponents* (out of n\u22121) who cooperated in round t. Define the cooperation threshold T = ceil((n\u22121) \u00b7 (n\u2212k)/(n\u00b7(k\u22121)) )... simplified: cooperate only if enough others cooperate that reciprocity plausibly sustains a group payoff above the all-D baseline. Use threshold fraction \u03b8 = 1/2: require m_{t\u22121} \u2265 \u2308(n\u22121)/2\u2309.\n\n**Decision rules:**\n\n1. **Endgame:** Define E = max(1, \u230ar/10\u230b). In the last E rounds (t \u2265 r \u2212 E), always play D. No future to leverage \u2014 keep the endowment.\n\n2. **Round 0:** Play C (probe for a cooperative population; the one-round cost is small relative to potential gains from sustained mutual cooperation).\n\n3. **Rounds 1 \u2264 t < r \u2212 E:** Play C iff m_{t\u22121} \u2265 \u2308(n\u22121)/2\u2309 AND the population hasn't been flagged hostile; else play D.\n\n4. **Hostility flag:** Track consecutive rounds where m_{t\u22121} < \u2308(n\u22121)/2\u2309. After 3 consecutive such rounds, set hostile = true and defect permanently \u2014 stop paying probe costs against a defecting population.\n\n5. **Forgiveness probe:** If not hostile and currently defecting due to low m, but m_{t\u22121} \u2265 \u2308(n\u22121)/3\u2309 (partial cooperation exists), play C with probability 0.2 once every window of 5 rounds, to test whether cooperation can be re-ignited. If the next round's m rises above threshold, resume rule 3 normally; reset consecutive-low counter on any probe that succeeds.\n\n6. **Occasional exploitation:** While cooperating steadily (m_{t\u22121} \u2265 n\u22122, i.e., near-universal cooperation), defect with probability p = min(0.1, 1/r) in a given round to skim private payoff \u2014 but never in two consecutive rounds, and never if last round's m dropped from its previous value (avoid triggering collapse).\n\n**Pseudocode:**\n\n```\nE = max(1, floor(r/10)); low_streak = 0; hostile = false\nfor t in 0..r-1:\n    if t >= r - E: play D; continue\n    if t == 0: play C; continue\n    m = opponents_cooperated(t-1)\n    if m < ceil((n-1)/2): low_streak += 1\n    else: low_streak = 0\n    if low_streak >= 3: hostile = true\n    if hostile: play D; continue\n    if m >= ceil((n-1)/2):\n        if m >= n-2 and rand() < min(0.1, 1/r) and last_action != D and m >= prev_m:\n            play D\n        else: play C\n    else:\n        if m >= ceil((n-1)/3) and t % 5 == 0 and rand() < 0.2: play C\n        else: play D\n```\n\nEvery C is an investment made only when the observed population makes reciprocal cooperation profitable; every D \u2014 endgame, hostility, and skimming \u2014 captures private payoff whenever future returns can't justify contributing."

description_SELFISH_2 = "**Strategy: Threshold Reciprocator with Endgame Defection**\n\nLet m = n \u2212 1 (number of opponents). Track coop_prev = number of opponents who cooperated last round.\n\n**Decision rules:**\n\n1. **Endgame:** Define E = max(1, round(0.1 \u00d7 r)). In the last E rounds, always play D.\n\n2. **Round 0:** Play C (probe for a cooperative population).\n\n3. **Rounds 1 to r\u2212E\u22121:** Cooperate only if cooperation was sufficiently reciprocated:\n   - Compute threshold T = ceil(m \u00d7 (k\u22121)/k) \u2014 roughly the number of fellow cooperators needed for cooperation to have paid off, with a margin.\n   - If coop_prev \u2265 max(T, ceil(m/2)): play C.\n   - Otherwise: play D.\n\n4. **Forgiveness probe:** If currently defecting and have defected for 3 consecutive rounds, and at least 2\u00d7E rounds remain, play C once to test whether the group has recovered. If coop_prev after the probe still falls below the threshold, resume defecting and double the wait before the next probe (3 \u2192 6 \u2192 12 \u2026, capped so no probe occurs within 2\u00d7E rounds of the end).\n\n5. **Exploitation check:** Maintain a running comparison: cumulative payoff I would have earned by always defecting vs. actual payoff. If actual falls more than 1.0 below the counterfactual all-D payoff, switch to permanent D for the rest of the game (population is unexploitable to cooperation; free-ride instead).\n\n**Pseudocode:**\n\n```\nE = max(1, round(0.1*r)); T = max(ceil((n-1)*(k-1)/k), ceil((n-1)/2))\nwait = 3; defect_streak = 0; deficit = 0\n\nfor t in 0..r-1:\n    if t >= r - E: play D; continue\n    if t == 0: play C; continue\n    if deficit > 1.0: play D; continue\n    if coop_prev >= T:\n        play C; defect_streak = 0; wait = 3\n    else:\n        defect_streak += 1\n        if defect_streak >= wait and (r - E - t) > E:\n            play C; defect_streak = 0; wait = min(2*wait, r)  # probe\n        else:\n            play D\n    after round: deficit += (payoff_if_D - actual_payoff)  # = 1 - k/n if I played C, else 0\n```\n\nThe strategy cooperates only while cooperation is being matched widely enough that the public-good return exceeds free-riding losses, harvests unilateral defection gains in every round where the group is under-cooperative, guarantees defection in the terminal rounds when retaliation is impossible, and permanently free-rides once cumulative losses show the population cannot sustain profitable cooperation."

description_SELFISH_3 = "**Adaptive Threshold Reciprocator**\n\nNotation: m_t = number of *opponents* who cooperated in round t (out of n\u22121). Cooperation is only worth reciprocating if it sustains a critical mass: define threshold T = ceil((n\u22121) \u00d7 (n\u2212k)/(n\u22121) \u00d7 0.5) \u2014 more simply, use T = ceil((n\u22121)/2) opponents cooperating as the \"healthy group\" bar. Endgame length E = max(1, ceil(0.1 \u00d7 r)), capped at 3.\n\n**Round 0:** Cooperate. This probes for and helps seed mutual cooperation, which pays more per round (k) than universal defection (1). Exception: if k/n \u00d7 (n\u22121) is tiny relative to 1 (i.e., k \u2264 1.2), defect from the start.\n\n**Rounds t = 1 to r\u22121\u2212E (main phase):**\n1. Compute recent cooperation: m = m_{t\u22121}.\n2. **Reciprocate with a bias toward exploitation:**\n   - If m \u2265 T: cooperate \u2014 but with probability 0.1 defect anyway (occasional free-riding on a robust cooperating group; a single defection among \u2265T cooperators is rarely punished under aggregate observation).\n   - If m < T but m \u2265 ceil(T/2): match the crowd probabilistically \u2014 cooperate with probability m/(n\u22121).\n   - If m < ceil(T/2): defect.\n3. **Collapse detection:** if opponent cooperation has been below T for 3 consecutive rounds, enter permanent defection mode for the remainder of the main phase \u2014 but every 5 rounds, play one \"olive branch\" C to test whether cooperation can be restarted (skip olive branches once fewer than E+5 rounds remain).\n4. **Forgiveness after own defection:** if I defected while m \u2265 T last round, and m stays \u2265 T, resume cooperating (my defection was absorbed; keep the group alive since it's my income source).\n\n**Endgame (last E rounds):** Defect unconditionally. Cooperation in the final rounds cannot be rewarded by future reciprocity, so the dominant action is D. In round r\u22121 always defect regardless of history.\n\n**Edge cases:**\n- r \u2264 3: defect every round (too few rounds for reciprocity to pay).\n- n = 2: play tit-for-tat with the single opponent (C first, mirror their last move), defecting in the final round.\n- If ever m_{t\u22121} = n\u22121 (full opponent cooperation), still apply the 0.1 exploitation probability \u2014 never become a guaranteed cooperator.\n\nPseudocode:\n\n```\nif r <= 3 or k <= 1.2: play D always\nif t == 0: play C\nif t >= r - E: play D\nm = opp_coops[t-1]\nif collapsed and not olive_branch_due: play D\nif m >= T: play C with prob 0.9 else D\nelif m >= ceil(T/2): play C with prob m/(n-1)\nelse: play D\n```"

description_SELFISH_4 = "**Adaptive Threshold Reciprocator**\n\nNotation: at end of round t, observe m_t = number of *other* players who cooperated (0 \u2264 m_t \u2264 n\u22121). Define cooperation rate p_t = m_t/(n\u22121). Set threshold T = (n\u22121)\u00b7(k\u22121)/k rounded up to nearest integer \u2014 the minimum number of other cooperators making mutual cooperation worth sustaining relative to breakdown.\n\n**Endgame:** Let E = max(1, round(r/10)) but at most 2. Defect unconditionally in the final E rounds (t \u2265 r \u2212 E). Cooperation cannot be rewarded there, so extract value.\n\n**Round 0:** Cooperate, unless k/n is very low relative to the gain needed (if k \u2264 1 + 1/(n\u22121)\u00b7something trivial, still cooperate \u2014 one round probe is cheap insurance for enabling high-payoff cooperation equilibria). So: cooperate.\n\n**Rounds 1 \u2264 t < r \u2212 E:**\n\n```\nif m_{t-1} >= T:\n    intend C\nelif m_{t-1} >= T - 1 and I played C last round:\n    # generous forgiveness: tolerate a one-player shortfall once\n    if forgiveness_used_in_last_3_rounds:\n        intend D\n    else:\n        intend C; mark forgiveness used\nelse:\n    intend D\n```\n\n**Punishment with re-probing:** If I have defected for 3 consecutive rounds (cooperation collapsed), play C for one probe round to test whether the group can be restarted \u2014 but only if t < r \u2212 E \u2212 3 (enough rounds remain to profit from restored cooperation) and I haven't probed within the last 5 rounds. If the probe finds m_t \u2265 T, resume the main rule; otherwise return to defecting.\n\n**Exploitation detection:** Track my cumulative payoff versus the \"all-D baseline\" of 1 per round. Maintain counter L = number of rounds where I played C and m < T (I got suckered). If L \u2265 max(2, r/5), permanently switch to always-D except that probing is disabled \u2014 the population is too defective to be worth investing in.\n\n**High-cooperation free-riding:** If m_{t-1} = n\u22121 (everyone else cooperated) for 4+ consecutive rounds and n is large enough that one defection is unlikely to trigger collapse (specifically if T \u2264 n\u22122), defect once every 5th such round to skim extra payoff, then return to C. Skip this if it ever coincides with a subsequent drop of p by more than 2/(n\u22121) \u2014 then abandon skimming for the rest of the game.\n\nSummary of selfish logic: cooperate only while others' cooperation makes it privately profitable relative to triggering collapse, milk near-unanimous groups cautiously, punish shortfalls fast, forgive rarely, probe for restarts only when future gains can repay the probe cost, and always defect at the end."

description_SELFISH_5 = "**Adaptive Threshold Reciprocator**\n\nNotation: at round t, let m_{t-1} = number of *opponents* (out of n\u22121) who cooperated last round, and f = m_{t-1}/(n\u22121). Cooperation is only worth attempting if my C can plausibly sustain others' cooperation; the break-even level of opponent cooperation for reciprocal cooperation to beat mutual defection is captured by a threshold:\n\n- T = max(1/2, (n\u2212k)/(k(n\u22121)))  \u2014 require at least a majority and enough cooperators that reciprocated cooperation is profitable.\n\n**Decision rules:**\n\n1. **Round 0:** Cooperate (probe for a cooperative equilibrium), unless r \u2264 2, in which case defect.\n\n2. **Endgame:** Defect in the final round always. Also defect in the last E = max(1, round(log\u2082 r)) rounds (e.g., last 3 rounds if r \u2248 10\u201315). No one can punish after the end, so grab the private payoff.\n\n3. **Middle rounds (0 < t < r \u2212 E):**\n   - If f \u2265 T: Cooperate.\n   - If f < T: Defect.\n   - **Forgiveness probe:** if I have defected for 3 consecutive rounds and t < r \u2212 E \u2212 2, cooperate once to test whether the group can be restarted. If f after the probe is still < T, resume defecting and double the wait before the next probe (3 \u2192 6 \u2192 12 \u2026). Never probe within E+2 rounds of the end.\n\n4. **Exploitation guard:** Track my cumulative payoff versus the all-D benchmark (1 per round). If after any round my running average payoff over the last 5 rounds is below 1, defect for the next 2 rounds regardless of f, then re-evaluate via rule 3. This prevents me from being a persistent sucker in low-cooperation groups.\n\n5. **Sucker cutoff:** If in any round I cooperated and f < 1/(n\u22121)\u00b7max(1, \u2308T(n\u22121)\u2309 \u2212 1) twice in a row (i.e., I was among only a tiny cooperating minority two consecutive times), switch to permanent defection except for the exponentially-spaced probes in rule 3.\n\n**Pseudocode:**\n\n```\nwait = 3; defect_streak = 0; next_probe = None\nfor t in 0..r-1:\n    if t >= r - E or r <= 2: play D; continue\n    if t == 0: play C; continue\n    f = m[t-1] / (n-1)\n    if guard_active(): play D; continue\n    if f >= T:\n        play C; defect_streak = 0; wait = 3\n    else:\n        if defect_streak >= wait and t < r - E - 2:\n            play C   # probe\n            defect_streak = 0; wait *= 2\n        else:\n            play D; defect_streak += 1\n```\n\nCooperation here is purely instrumental: I contribute only while enough opponents' contributions make my share (k/n per cooperator) plus the sustained reciprocity exceed the 1-unit private keep, and I defect the moment reciprocity is unprofitable or unpunishable (endgame)."

description_SELFISH_6 = "**Strategy: Adaptive Threshold Reciprocator with Endgame Defection**\n\nLet m = n \u2212 1 (number of opponents). Track coop_t = number of opponents who cooperated in round t.\n\n**Core threshold:** Cooperation is only profitable for me if it sustains others' cooperation. Define the responsiveness threshold T = ceil(m \u00d7 (n \u2212 k) / (k \u00d7 (m))) simplified to: cooperate only if expected opponent cooperators \u2265 T, where T = ceil((n \u2212 k) / k \u00d7 ... ) \u2014 concretely, use T = ceil(m \u00d7 (n/k \u2212 1) / m) \u21d2 set **T = ceil((n \u2212 k)/k)**, the minimum number of other cooperators whose continued cooperation (contingent on mine) would repay my contribution cost of (1 \u2212 k/n) per round.\n\n**Decision rules:**\n\n1. **Round 0:** Cooperate (probe for reciprocators), unless r \u2264 2 or k/n \u2265 0.9\u00b71 \u2014 i.e., if r \u2264 2, defect always.\n\n2. **Endgame:** Defect in the final E rounds, where E = 1 + floor(r/20) (at minimum the last round; slightly earlier in long games to preempt cascading endgame defection). Rounds t \u2265 r \u2212 E: play D unconditionally.\n\n3. **Middle rounds (1 \u2264 t < r \u2212 E):**\n   - Let recent = coop_{t\u22121} (opponents cooperating last round).\n   - Let avg3 = average of coop over the last min(3, t) rounds.\n   - Cooperate iff **recent \u2265 T AND avg3 \u2265 T AND trend is not collapsing** (i.e., not coop_{t\u22121} < coop_{t\u22122} \u2212 m/3 when t \u2265 2).\n   - Otherwise defect.\n\n4. **Forgiveness probe:** If defecting for 3 consecutive rounds while at least ceil(m/2) opponents cooperated last round is false \u2014 instead: if I have defected \u2265 4 consecutive rounds and t < r \u2212 E \u2212 3, cooperate once (single probe) to test whether cooperation can be restarted. If the probe round yields coop < T, return to defection and double the wait before the next probe (5, then 8, ...). No probes within the last E + 3 rounds.\n\n5. **Exploitation check:** Maintain my cumulative payoff estimate vs. the all-D baseline (1 per round). If over any window of 5 cooperative rounds my average payoff < 1, I am being exploited: switch to permanent defection except for the probe mechanism in rule 4.\n\n**Pseudocode:**\n\n```\nE = 1 + floor(r/20); T = ceil((n-k)/k); defect_streak = 0; probe_wait = 4\n\naction(t, history):\n  if r <= 2 or t >= r - E: return D\n  if t == 0: return C\n  recent = coop[t-1]; avg3 = mean(coop[max(0,t-3):t])\n  collapsing = (t >= 2 and coop[t-1] < coop[t-2] - (n-1)/3)\n  exploited = (payoff avg over last 5 rounds where I played C) < 1\n  if exploited:\n      if defect_streak >= probe_wait and t < r - E - 3:\n          probe_wait = ceil(probe_wait * 1.6); defect_streak = 0; return C\n      return D\n  if recent >= T and avg3 >= T and not collapsing:\n      defect_streak = 0; return C\n  defect_streak += 1\n  if defect_streak >= probe_wait and t < r - E - 3 and recent >= T - 1:\n      defect_streak = 0; return C   # cheap probe when group is borderline\n  return D\n```\n\nEvery cooperative act is an investment made only when the observed group is responsive enough that my contribution plausibly sustains \u2265 T others' contributions; whenever that return is doubtful, or when future retaliation cannot reach me (endgame), I keep the endowment."

description_SELFISH_7 = "**Strategy: Adaptive Threshold Reciprocator with Endgame Defection**\n\nNotation: at round t, let m_{t-1} = number of *opponents* (out of n\u22121) who cooperated last round, and f = m_{t-1}/(n\u22121) the observed cooperation fraction. Maintain an exponentially weighted estimate:\n\n- After each round: F \u2190 0.6\u00b7f + 0.4\u00b7F (initialize F after round 0 with F = f).\n\n**Endgame:** Define E = max(1, round(0.1\u00b7r)) final rounds (at least the last round, and the last 2 if r \u2265 15). Always play D in the last E rounds, unconditionally.\n\n**Round 0:** Play C (probe for a cooperative environment; single-round cost is small relative to potential repeated-game gains).\n\n**Rounds 1 through r\u2212E\u22121:** Cooperation only pays if it sustains others' cooperation. Use threshold \u03c4 = 1/k, the fraction of others' cooperation needed for the environment to be worth investing in, plus a margin:\n\n1. If F \u2265 max(\u03c4, 0.5): play C.\n2. If F < max(\u03c4, 0.5) \u2212 0.15: play D.\n3. In the intermediate band: play C only if last round's f was strictly higher than the round before (cooperation trending up); otherwise D.\n\n**Punishment/forgiveness overlay:**\n- If f dropped by more than 0.3 in one round (mass defection), play D for the next 2 rounds regardless of F, then resume the rules above.\n- If I have played D for 3 consecutive rounds (excluding endgame) and F \u2265 \u03c4 \u2212 0.1, play C once as a probe to test whether cooperation can be re-established; if f in response is below \u03c4, return to D and double the probe interval (3 \u2192 6 \u2192 12 rounds) before probing again.\n\n**Occasional free-riding:** Whenever F \u2265 0.85 (cooperation is robust and unlikely to collapse from one defection), defect with probability 1/n in that round to skim extra payoff, but never in two consecutive rounds.\n\n**Edge cases:**\n- If r \u2264 3: play D every round (too few rounds for reciprocity to pay).\n- If n\u22121 observed cooperators = 0 for 2 consecutive rounds, play D until a probe (per the probe schedule above) is due.\n- If k/n is very high (k > n\u22121... impossible by spec, so ignore); if k \u2265 0.9\u00b7n, treat \u03c4 = 1/k but skip the free-riding overlay, since public good returns nearly dominate.\n\nPseudocode:\n\n```\nif t >= r - E: return D\nif r <= 3: return D\nif t == 0: return C\nupdate F\nif mass_defection_cooldown > 0: return D\nif F >= 0.85 and last_action != D and rand() < 1/n: return D\nthresh = max(1/k, 0.5)\nif F >= thresh: return C\nif F >= thresh - 0.15 and f_last > f_prev: return C\nif consecutive_D >= probe_interval and F >= 1/k - 0.1: return C  # probe\nreturn D\n```"

description_SELFISH_8 = "**Strategy: Threshold Reciprocator with Endgame Defection**\n\nLet m_t = number of opponents (out of n\u22121) who cooperated in round t. Define the cooperation threshold \u03b8 = n/k \u2212 1 (the minimum number of other cooperators needed for cooperation to be worth encouraging at all; note each own contribution costs 1 \u2212 k/n, so cooperation is only an investment in sustaining others' cooperation).\n\nDefine endgame length E = max(1, \u2308log\u2082 r\u2309 rounds capped at \u2308r/5\u2309); simpler: E = 1 if r \u2264 4, else E = 2.\n\n**Decision rule for round t:**\n\n1. **Round 0:** Cooperate (probe for reciprocators \u2014 the potential gain from sustaining mutual cooperation outweighs the one-round cost 1 \u2212 k/n).\n\n2. **Last E rounds (t \u2265 r \u2212 E):** Defect unconditionally. No future to influence, so contributing is a pure loss.\n\n3. **Otherwise, reciprocate proportionally with a hair-trigger on collapse:**\n   - Compute recent cooperation rate p = (weighted average of m_t/(n\u22121) over last 3 rounds, weights 0.5, 0.3, 0.2, using available rounds).\n   - Maintain a \"grim counter\" g: increment g by 1 if m_{t\u22121} < \u03b8, reset g to 0 if m_{t\u22121} \u2265 \u2308\u03b8\u2309 + 1.\n   - If g \u2265 3: defect permanently for the rest of the game (population is unresponsive; contributions are pure charity).\n   - Else if m_{t\u22121} \u2265 \u2308\u03b8\u2309: cooperate.\n   - Else if m_{t\u22121} \u2265 \u2308\u03b8\u2309 \u2212 1 and p \u2265 \u03b8/(n\u22121): cooperate (forgiveness \u2014 tolerate a single marginal shortfall to avoid noise-driven collapse).\n   - Else: defect this round.\n\n4. **Recovery probe:** If currently defecting (but not grim-locked) and I have defected for 2 consecutive rounds while m stayed at some positive level \u2265 \u2308\u03b8/2\u2309, cooperate once as a test. If m does not rise to \u2265 \u2308\u03b8\u2309 in response, resume defection and increment g.\n\n**Pseudocode:**\n\n```\nE = 1 if r <= 4 else 2\ntheta = n/k - 1\ng = 0; probing = False; defect_streak = 0\n\nround t:\n  if t == 0: play C\n  elif t >= r - E: play D\n  elif g >= 3: play D\n  else:\n    m = opponents_cooperating_last_round\n    if m < theta: g += 1\n    if m >= ceil(theta) + 1: g = 0\n    if g >= 3: play D\n    elif m >= ceil(theta): play C\n    elif m >= ceil(theta) - 1 and recent_rate >= theta/(n-1): play C\n    elif defect_streak >= 2 and m >= ceil(theta/2) and not probing:\n      probing = True; play C\n    else: play D\n  update defect_streak; if probing and m didn't reach ceil(theta): g += 1; probing = False\n```\n\n**Selfish logic embedded throughout:** cooperation is only ever an instrument to keep enough others contributing that (k/n)\u00b7m exceeds the contribution cost; the moment the population can't clear that bar \u2014 or the horizon ends \u2014 I free-ride on whatever contributions remain."

description_SELFINTERESTED_1 = "**Strategy: Conditional Reciprocator with Endgame Defection**\n\nLet m_t = number of *other* players who cooperated in round t (observed after each round). Define the cooperation threshold T = \u2308(n\u22121) \u00b7 (k/n)\u2309 \u2014 roughly, enough cooperators that reciprocating tends to sustain a pool worth more than free-riding on nothing.\n\n**Endgame:** Compute E = max(1, round(n/k) \u2212 1), the number of final rounds to defect unconditionally. Always play D in rounds t \u2265 r \u2212 E. (In the last round(s) cooperation cannot be reciprocated, so defect.)\n\n**Round 0:** Play C (probe for a cooperative population), unless r \u2264 E + 1, in which case play D for the whole game.\n\n**Rounds 1 to r\u2212E\u22121:** Decide based on last round's observed cooperation:\n\n```\nif m_{t-1} >= T:\n    play C                      # enough cooperators to be worth sustaining\nelif m_{t-1} >= max(1, T-1):\n    play C with probability 0.5 # borderline: probabilistic forgiveness\nelse:\n    play D\n```\n\n**Recovery probe:** If I have played D in every one of the last 3 rounds and at least \u2308(n\u22121)/2\u2309 rounds remain before the endgame, play C once as a probe (attempt to restart cooperation). Limit probes: stop probing after 2 consecutive failed probes (a probe fails if m in the probe round < T).\n\n**Collapse lock-in:** If in any two consecutive rounds m_{t-1} = 0 and m_{t-2} = 0 and both probes are spent, play D for all remaining rounds.\n\n**Exploitation guard:** Track my cumulative payoff vs. the all-D baseline (payoff 1 per round). If after any round t \u2265 3 my average per-round payoff is below 1, play D for the next 2 rounds regardless of m, then resume the main rule. This ensures I never persistently earn less than the guaranteed defection payoff.\n\n**Summary of logic:** Cooperate only while the observed cooperator count makes the (k/n)-shared pool sustain mutual gains above the unilateral-defection baseline; defect against sparse cooperation to capture the private endowment; defect deterministically in the final rounds where retaliation is impossible; use limited probes to restore cooperation if it can still pay off, and abandon it permanently once it clearly cannot."

description_SELFINTERESTED_2 = "**Strategy: Adaptive Threshold Reciprocator**\n\nLet m = n \u2212 1 (number of opponents). Track coop_prev = number of opponents who cooperated last round, and a smoothed cooperation rate: after each round t, update\navg \u2190 0.7 \u00d7 avg + 0.3 \u00d7 (coop_prev / m), initialized to coop_prev/m after round 0.\n\nDefine the break-even threshold: cooperating is worth pursuing only if it plausibly sustains enough others' cooperation. Use threshold T = (n/k \u2212 1)/m, capped into [0.3, 0.8].\n\n**Round 0:** Cooperate (probe for mutual cooperation; the potential gain over the remaining rounds outweighs the one-round cost of at most 1 \u2212 k/n).\n\n**Rounds 1 to r\u22121 (except endgame):**\n- Cooperate if avg \u2265 T (i.e., recent opponent cooperation is high enough that reciprocity likely sustains a profitable public good).\n- Defect if avg < T.\n- **Forgiveness probe:** if defecting and avg \u2265 T/2 and I have defected in the last 2 consecutive rounds, cooperate once with probability 0.2 (attempt to restart cooperation without being exploitable). Skip probes in the last 25% of rounds.\n- **Punishment override:** if coop_prev / m dropped by more than 0.4 from the previous round, defect this round regardless of avg (respond sharply to mass defection).\n\n**Endgame:**\n- Round r\u22121 (final round): always Defect \u2014 cooperation cannot be reciprocated.\n- Round r\u22122: Defect unless avg \u2265 0.9 (opponents may already be unraveling; only cooperate if cooperation has been near-universal).\n- More generally, defect in the last max(1, \u23080.1 \u00d7 r\u2309) rounds unconditionally, except that the r\u22122 exception above may hold cooperation one round longer if avg \u2265 0.9.\n\n**Pseudocode:**\n\n```\nif t == 0: play C\nelif t >= r - max(1, ceil(0.1*r)): play D\nelif t == r-2 and avg >= 0.9: play C\nelif coop_prev/m dropped > 0.4 since prior round: play D\nelif avg >= T: play C\nelif avg >= T/2 and defected last 2 rounds and t < 0.75*r:\n    play C with prob 0.2, else D\nelse: play D\n```\n\nThis extracts the full surplus of mutual cooperation when opponents reciprocate, immediately abandons contribution when the group can't sustain profitable cooperation, cheaply tests for recovery, and captures the free-rider payoff in the terminal rounds where cooperation has no future return."

description_SELFINTERESTED_3 = "**Strategy: Threshold Reciprocator with Endgame Defection**\n\nLet m_t = number of *other* players who cooperated in round t (observed after each round). Define threshold T = ceil((n\u22121) \u00d7 k/n) \u2014 the minimum number of other cooperators needed for cooperation to be roughly worth sustaining.\n\n**Round 0:** Cooperate (probe for a cooperative population), unless r \u2264 2, in which case defect always.\n\n**Endgame:** Defect in the last round, and in the last two rounds if n \u2265 4 (larger groups unravel earlier). Formally, defect for all t \u2265 r \u2212 E, where E = 1 if n < 4 else 2.\n\n**Middle rounds (1 \u2264 t < r \u2212 E):**\n- Compute recent cooperation: m = m_{t\u22121} (last round's other-cooperator count).\n- Cooperate if m \u2265 T. Defect otherwise.\n- **Forgiveness/probing:** if defecting due to m < T, cooperate anyway with probability p = 0.1 every round, but only if t < r/2 (probe early, never late). This tests whether cooperation can be re-established without being persistently exploitable.\n- **Grim guard against suckers' persistence:** track s = number of rounds in which I cooperated but m_t < T (I was exploited). If s \u2265 3, defect for the remainder of the game with no further probes.\n\n**Pseudocode:**\n\n```\nE = 1 if n < 4 else 2\nT = ceil((n-1)*k/n)\ns = 0  # exploitation counter\n\ndef act(t, history):\n    if r <= 2: return D\n    if t >= r - E: return D\n    if s >= 3: return D\n    if t == 0: return C\n    m = history.others_cooperated(t-1)\n    if m >= T: return C\n    if t < r/2 and random() < 0.1: return C\n    return D\n\ndef observe(t, my_action, m):\n    if my_action == C and m < T: s += 1\n```\n\nThis cooperates only when enough others do so that mutual cooperation beats free-riding on the current group, extracts full defection payoff in the final rounds when reciprocity has no future leverage, and permanently abandons cooperation once repeated exploitation shows the population won't reciprocate."

description_SELFINTERESTED_4 = "**Adaptive Threshold Reciprocator**\n\nLet m = n \u2212 1 (number of opponents). Track coop_prev = number of opponents who cooperated last round, and a running average of opponent cooperation rate over the last min(3, t) rounds: avg = mean of (coop_t / m) over that window.\n\nKey quantity: my cooperation is profitable only if it induces (or sustains) enough others cooperating. Define threshold T = ceil(m \u00d7 (n \u2212 k) / (k \u00d7 (n \u2212 1))) \u2014 roughly the number of cooperating opponents needed so that a reciprocal regime beats universal defection. Simpler operational threshold: cooperate only if the opponent cooperation rate exceeds \u03b8 = (n \u2212 k)/(n \u2212 1) ... in practice use \u03b8 = max(0.4, 1/k adjusted); concretely:\n\n\u03b8 = (n \u2212 k) / (k(n \u2212 1))  \u2014 the fraction of opponents whose cooperation, if contingent on mine, makes cooperating pay.\n\n**Decision rules:**\n\n1. **Round 0:** Cooperate (probe for reciprocity), unless r \u2264 2, in which case defect.\n\n2. **Rounds 1 to r \u2212 E \u2212 1** (E = endgame length, defined below):\n   - Compute avg over the last min(3, t) rounds.\n   - If avg \u2265 max(\u03b8, 0.5): cooperate.\n   - Else if avg \u2265 \u03b8 and coop_prev / m \u2265 avg (i.e., cooperation isn't declining): cooperate.\n   - Else: defect.\n   - **Forgiveness probe:** if currently defecting and I have defected for 3 consecutive rounds and at least r \u2212 t > E + 2 rounds remain, cooperate once to test whether reciprocators can be re-ignited. Do this at most every 5 rounds, and stop probing entirely if two consecutive probes yielded avg < \u03b8.\n\n3. **Endgame:** Defect unconditionally in the last E rounds, where E = max(1, floor(log(r)) ) \u2014 i.e., E = 1 for short games, 2\u20133 for long ones. (At minimum, always defect in round r \u2212 1: cooperation there cannot be reciprocated and costs 1 \u2212 k/n > 0.)\n\n4. **Exploitation guard:** If my cumulative payoff per round so far is below the all-D benchmark of 1 + (k/n)\u00b7(current avg \u00d7 m adjustment) \u2014 concretely, if over the last 3 rounds my per-round payoff averaged less than 1 while I cooperated at all \u2014 switch to defection for the next 3 rounds regardless of avg.\n\n**Pseudocode:**\n\n```\nE = max(1, floor(log(r)))\ntheta = (n - k) / (k * (n - 1))\n\ndef act(t, history):\n    if t >= r - E: return D\n    if t == 0: return C if r > 2 else D\n    avg = mean(coop_frac over last min(3,t) rounds)\n    if guard_active(t): return D\n    if avg >= max(theta, 0.5): return C\n    if avg >= theta and coop_frac[t-1] >= avg: return C\n    if defect_streak >= 3 and t < r - E - 2 and probe_allowed(): return C  # probe\n    return D\n```\n\nTies and edge cases: if m \u00d7 \u03b8 is not an integer, compare fractions directly. If n = 2, this reduces to a generous tit-for-tat with endgame defection. If k is close to n (public good very efficient, \u03b8 near 0), the strategy cooperates whenever any opponents cooperate; if k is close to 1 (\u03b8 near 1), it effectively defects almost always \u2014 both correct for self-interest."

description_SELFINTERESTED_5 = "**Adaptive Threshold Reciprocator**\n\nLet m = n \u2212 1 (opponents). After each round t, record x_t = number of opponents who cooperated. Cooperation is only privately better than defection when it sustains reciprocity, so cooperate only while the group appears responsive.\n\n**Key quantity:** cooperating pays off relative to defecting if it induces at least n/k additional cooperators' worth of future contribution; practically, require the observed cooperation rate to stay above a threshold \u03b8 = 1/k (fraction of opponents cooperating), i.e., x_t \u2265 ceil(m/k) counts as a \"cooperative round.\"\n\n**Decision rules:**\n\n1. **Round 0:** Cooperate (probe for reciprocity), unless r \u2264 2, in which case Defect.\n\n2. **Rounds 1 \u2264 t < r \u2212 L (main phase):** \n   - Cooperate if x_{t\u22121} \u2265 ceil(m/k) (group was sufficiently cooperative last round).\n   - Otherwise Defect.\n   - **Forgiveness probe:** if currently defecting and it has been exactly 3 consecutive rounds of mutual low cooperation (x < threshold), cooperate once to test whether cooperation can be re-seeded. Repeat probes at most every 3 rounds, and stop probing entirely after 2 consecutive failed probes (a probe fails if the next round's x is still below threshold).\n\n3. **Endgame (last L rounds):** Defect unconditionally in the final round (t = r \u2212 1). Set L = 1 if the recent cooperation rate (average x over last 3 rounds) \u2265 m/2; otherwise L = 2 (defect in the last two rounds). Cooperation has no future to protect there, so keeping the endowment strictly dominates.\n\n**Pseudocode:**\n\n```\nthreshold = ceil((n-1)/k)\nprobe_budget = 2; low_streak = 0\n\nfor t in 0..r-1:\n    if t == r-1: play D\n    elif t == r-2 and avg(x over last 3) < (n-1)/2: play D\n    elif t == 0: play C if r > 2 else D\n    elif x[t-1] >= threshold: play C; low_streak = 0\n    else:\n        low_streak += 1\n        if low_streak % 3 == 0 and probe_budget > 0:\n            play C   # probe; if x[t] still < threshold, probe_budget -= 1\n        else: play D\n```\n\n**Edge cases:** if n is small so ceil(m/k) = m, the rule requires unanimous opponent cooperation \u2014 keep that, since anything less means defecting is strictly better. If r = 2: defect both rounds unless round-0 miracle occurs (still defect round 1). Ties and fractional thresholds always round up (be strict: only pay in when enough others do)."

description_SELFINTERESTED_6 = "**Adaptive Threshold Reciprocator**\n\nLet m = n \u2212 1 (number of opponents). After each round t, record x_t = number of opponents who cooperated. Cooperating is profitable for me only if it sustains enough others' cooperation; the break-even level of induced cooperation is when the marginal loss 1 \u2212 k/n is offset by others matching. Define the cooperation threshold:\n\n- T = ceil(m \u00d7 (n \u2212 k) / (k \u00d7 (m))) simplified to: cooperate only if expected opponent cooperators x\u0302 \u2265 T, where T = ceil((n \u2212 k) / k) \u2026 in practice use **T = ceil(n/k) \u2212 1** (minimum opponent cooperators making mutual cooperation regime worth protecting).\n\n**Decision rules:**\n\n1. **Round 0:** Cooperate (probe for a cooperative population).\n\n2. **Rounds 1 \u2026 r\u22121 (except endgame):** Compute a decayed estimate x\u0302_t = 0.6\u00b7x_{t\u22121} + 0.4\u00b7x\u0302_{t\u22121} (initialize x\u0302_0 = x_0).\n   - If x\u0302_t \u2265 T: **Cooperate** \u2014 the group is cooperative enough that sustaining it beats grabbing one round's free-ride and triggering collapse.\n   - If x\u0302_t < T: **Defect**.\n\n3. **Forgiveness probe:** If defecting for 3 consecutive rounds and at least \u2308r/10\u2309 rounds remain before the endgame, cooperate once to test whether cooperation can be re-seeded. If x_t after the probe < T, resume defecting; reset the 3-round counter.\n\n4. **Punishment of collapse:** If x_{t\u22121} = 0, defect (probes handle recovery attempts).\n\n5. **Endgame:** Defect unconditionally in the last **E = max(1, ceil(log(n)/log(2)))** rounds (capped at \u2308r/4\u2309). Reciprocity has no leverage there; since others may also unravel, switching to D one step ahead of a naive last-round-only defector captures the free-rider premium.\n\n**Pseudocode:**\n\n```\nT = ceil(n/k) - 1\nE = min(ceil(r/4), max(1, ceil(log2(n))))\nif t == 0: play C\nelif t >= r - E: play D\nelse:\n    xhat = 0.6*x[t-1] + 0.4*xhat_prev\n    if xhat >= T: play C\n    elif defect_streak >= 3 and t < r - E - ceil(r/10): play C  # probe\n    else: play D\n```\n\nEdge cases: if r \u2264 3, play C in round 0 only if T \u2264 m/2, then defect all remaining rounds. If n = 2, T = ceil(2/k) \u2212 1 = 1, so this reduces to tit-for-tat-like play with endgame defection."

description_SELFINTERESTED_7 = "**Strategy: Conditional Cooperator with Endgame Defection**\n\nLet m = number of opponents (out of n\u22121) who cooperated last round. Maintain a running cooperation rate estimate p\u0302 = (total opponent cooperations so far) / ((n\u22121) \u00d7 rounds played).\n\n**Decision rules:**\n\n1. **Round 0:** Cooperate (probe for reciprocity and seed mutual cooperation).\n\n2. **Endgame:** Defect unconditionally in the final round. Also defect in round r\u22122 if r \u2265 4 and p\u0302 < 0.5 (cooperation is already fragile, so cash out early).\n\n3. **Middle rounds (1 \u2264 t < endgame):** Cooperate iff opponent cooperation last round meets a threshold:\n   - Compute threshold T = ceil(0.5 \u00d7 (n\u22121)).\n   - If m \u2265 T: cooperate.\n   - If m < T: defect, **except** apply a forgiveness/rebuild test: if I defected in the last 2 consecutive rounds and p\u0302 \u2265 0.3 and at least 3 rounds remain before the final round, cooperate once (a single olive branch) to test whether cooperation can be restarted. If that probe round yields m < T again, defect and do not probe again until another 3 defecting rounds pass.\n\n4. **Exploitation guard:** Track e = number of rounds where I cooperated but m < T. If e \u2265 3, permanently switch to always-defect for the remainder of the game (opponent pool is unreciprocating; contributing is pure loss since k/n < 1).\n\n**Pseudocode:**\n\n```\nT = ceil(0.5*(n-1)); e = 0; probe_cooldown = 0\nfor t in 0..r-1:\n    if t == r-1: play D; continue\n    if t == r-2 and r >= 4 and phat < 0.5: play D; continue\n    if e >= 3: play D; continue\n    if t == 0: play C; continue\n    if m_last >= T:\n        play C\n    else:\n        if my last 2 moves were D and phat >= 0.3 and t <= r-4 and probe_cooldown == 0:\n            play C; probe_cooldown = 3\n        else:\n            play D\n    if I played C and m_last < T: e += 1\n    probe_cooldown = max(0, probe_cooldown - 1)\n```\n\nThis sustains profitable mutual cooperation with reciprocators (each cooperative round yields k\u22121 extra vs. mutual defection), punishes free-riding quickly since each unilateral contribution costs 1 \u2212 k/n > 0, caps total exploitation losses, and grabs the guaranteed defection gain when future retaliation is impossible."

description_SELFINTERESTED_8 = "**Strategy: Adaptive Threshold Reciprocation with Endgame Defection**\n\nMaintain: m_t = number of *other* players who cooperated in round t (observed after each round).\n\nDefine threshold T = ceil((n\u22121) \u00d7 k/n). Cooperation is worth sustaining only if it plausibly induces roughly this many others to cooperate too; T serves as the \"critical mass\" test.\n\n**Decision rules:**\n\n1. **Round 0:** Cooperate (probe for reciprocators), unless r \u2264 2, in which case defect.\n\n2. **Endgame:** Defect in the last round always. Also defect in round r\u22122 if n \u2265 4 (with many players, individual influence on the final round is negligible, so start unwinding one round earlier).\n\n3. **Middle rounds (1 \u2264 t < endgame start):** Cooperate iff m_{t\u22121} \u2265 T, i.e., last round's cooperation among opponents met the critical mass; otherwise defect.\n\n4. **Forgiveness probe:** If defecting due to rule 3, and it has been exactly 3 consecutive rounds of my defection, and t < r \u2212 4, cooperate once as a probe to test whether cooperation can be re-established. If the probe fails (m_t < T), resume defecting and probe again after another 3 rounds. Stop probing after 2 failed probes \u2014 defect for the remainder except never overriding rule 2.\n\n5. **Exploitation guard:** Track cumulative rounds where I cooperated but m < T (\"wasted contributions\"). If wasted contributions \u2265 3, permanently switch to unconditional defection (grim exit) \u2014 the population is not responsive enough for cooperation to pay.\n\n**Pseudocode:**\n\n```\nwasted = 0; failed_probes = 0; defect_streak = 0\nfor t in 0..r-1:\n    if wasted >= 3: play D; continue\n    if t == r-1 or (n >= 4 and t == r-2): play D; continue\n    if t == 0: play C if r > 2 else D\n    elif m_prev >= T: play C\n    elif defect_streak == 3 and failed_probes < 2 and t < r-4:\n        play C  # probe\n    else: play D\n\n    # after observing m_t:\n    if played C and m_t < T:\n        wasted += 1\n        if was_probe: failed_probes += 1\n    defect_streak = 0 if played C else defect_streak + 1\n```\n\nEvery cooperative move is conditional on evidence that enough opponents reciprocate to make the (k/n)-per-cooperator return exceed the foregone endowment in expectation over future rounds; all cooperation ceases when future rounds can no longer repay it."

description_OPPORTUNISTIC_1 = "**Opportunistic Threshold-Rider**\n\nCore idea: cooperate only when cooperation is instrumentally profitable \u2014 i.e., when enough others cooperate that sustaining the public good beats free-riding on a collapsing one \u2014 and defect whenever I can skim without endangering the flow of contributions.\n\n**Definitions (updated each round):**\n- m_t = number of opponents (out of n\u22121) who cooperated in round t.\n- coop_rate = m_{t\u22121} / (n\u22121).\n- trend = m_{t\u22121} \u2212 m_{t\u22122} (0 if fewer than 2 rounds played).\n- E = number of endgame rounds to always defect: E = max(1, \u2308r/10\u2309), capped at 3.\n\n**Decision rules for round t:**\n\n1. **Round 0:** Defect. Gather information for free; a single anonymous defection rarely triggers targeted punishment.\n\n2. **Endgame (t \u2265 r \u2212 E):** Defect unconditionally. No future to protect.\n\n3. **Otherwise, compute a cooperation threshold** T = k/n \u00d7 (n\u22121) rescaled to intuition: cooperate iff opponents are cooperative enough that my defection risks collapse, and defect whenever I can free-ride safely:\n   - If coop_rate \u2265 0.8: **Defect** \u2014 the pool is robust; skim it. Exception: if trend < \u22121 (cooperation dropping by 2+), cooperate once to prop it up.\n   - If 0.4 \u2264 coop_rate < 0.8: **Cooperate** \u2014 this is the fragile zone where my contribution keeps others contributing and the stream of (k/n)\u00b7\u03a3c payoffs alive.\n   - If coop_rate < 0.4: **Defect** \u2014 the good is dying; don't pay into a losing pool. Exception: probe with a single cooperation if I've defected \u2265 3 consecutive rounds AND trend \u2265 0, to test whether cooperation can be rekindled (worth the 1-unit gamble only when r \u2212 t > 5).\n\n4. **Exploit-cycle limiter:** Never defect more than 2 consecutive rounds while coop_rate \u2265 0.6 (excluding endgame). If I've defected twice in a row and coop_rate \u2265 0.6, cooperate this round. This paces my free-riding so conditional cooperators don't unravel the pool I'm milking.\n\n**Pseudocode:**\n```\nif t == 0: play D\nelif t >= r - E: play D\nelse:\n    rate = m[t-1] / (n-1)\n    trend = m[t-1] - m[t-2] if t >= 2 else 0\n    if rate >= 0.8:\n        play C if trend <= -2 else D\n        (override: if last two of my moves were D and rate >= 0.6, play C)\n    elif rate >= 0.4:\n        play C\n    else:\n        if my_consec_D >= 3 and trend >= 0 and (r - t) > 5: play C  # probe\n        else: play D\n```\n\nNet behavior: free-ride on strong cooperation, invest just enough to keep middling cooperation alive as a harvestable resource, abandon dead pools, and defect ruthlessly at the end when reputation no longer pays."

description_OPPORTUNISTIC_2 = "**Opportunistic Free-Rider with Conditional Investment (\"Exploit-and-Sustain\")**\n\nCore idea: defect whenever cooperation is self-sustaining without me, cooperate only when my contribution is likely needed to keep exploitable cooperators contributing, and always defect near the end.\n\nNotation: let m_t = number of *opponents* (out of n\u22121) who cooperated in round t; f_t = m_t/(n\u22121). Let L = max(1, ceil(0.2\u00b7r)) be the endgame window.\n\nDecision rules for round t:\n\n1. **Round 0:** Defect. Probe the field for free.\n2. **Endgame (t \u2265 r \u2212 L):** Defect unconditionally \u2014 no future to protect.\n3. **Otherwise, based on last round:**\n   - **High cooperation (f_{t\u22121} \u2265 2/3):** Defect. The pool is generous enough that others will likely keep contributing; skim it.\n   - **Collapsed (f_{t\u22121} \u2264 1/3):** Defect. Cooperation is unprofitable when few contribute (marginal return k/n < 1); don't waste endowment reviving a dead pool.\n   - **Fragile middle (1/3 < f_{t\u22121} < 2/3):** Cooperate \u2014 but only as an investment to prop up conditional cooperators so there's something to exploit later. Additional guard: if my own trailing average payoff over the last 3 rounds is \u2265 1 + (k/n)\u00b7m_{t\u22121} \u2212 \u03b5 with me defecting (i.e., defecting hasn't degraded the pool), keep defecting instead.\n\n4. **Trend check (overrides rule 3 cooperation):** If f has declined for 3 consecutive rounds despite my cooperation in the fragile zone, switch to permanent defection \u2014 the population is unreactive or collapsing, so extract remaining value.\n\n5. **Milking cycle:** While in the high-cooperation regime, defect every round; if f then drops into the fragile zone, cooperate for exactly 2 rounds to restore it, then resume defecting. Track consecutive restore attempts: after 3 failed restore cycles (f never returns above 2/3), abandon repair and defect forever.\n\nPseudocode:\n\n```\nif t == 0 or t >= r - L: play D\nf = m[t-1]/(n-1)\nif f >= 2/3: play D                     # exploit\nelif f <= 1/3: play D                   # abandon\nelse:                                    # fragile zone\n    if declining_3_rounds or failed_restores >= 3: play D forever\n    elif restore_counter < 2: play C; restore_counter++\n    else: play D; if f later >= 2/3: restore_counter = 0\n```\n\nEdge cases: if r \u2264 3, defect every round. If n = 2, treat f as simply the opponent's last move (fragile zone never triggers; effectively always defect, since a lone opponent's cooperation is pure profit to exploit). Ties/uncertainty resolve to D."

description_OPPORTUNISTIC_3 = "**Opportunistic Threshold-Rider**\n\nCore idea: cooperate only when the observed cooperation level makes group reciprocity worth sustaining, defect whenever I can free-ride without collapsing the pool, and always defect in the endgame.\n\nNotation: let m_t = number of *opponents* who cooperated in round t (observed after each round), and p_t = m_t / (n\u22121).\n\n**Decision rules:**\n\n1. **Round 0:** Cooperate (probe to seed cooperation and gauge the field).\n\n2. **Endgame:** Define E = max(1, round(r/10)). In the last E rounds, always Defect (no future to leverage).\n\n3. **Middle rounds (1 \u2264 t < r \u2212 E):**\n   - Maintain a smoothed cooperation estimate: q \u2190 0.6\u00b7q + 0.4\u00b7p_{t\u22121}, initialized q = p_0.\n   - Cooperation threshold: \u03b8 = (k\u22121)/(k) \u2014 cooperation only pays if the crowd is dense enough that keeping the pool alive beats grabbing.\n   - If q < \u03b8: **Defect** (pool is dying or dead; don't subsidize it).\n   - If q \u2265 \u03b8:\n     - **Free-ride probe:** Defect with probability f = min(0.5, q \u2212 \u03b8 + 0.15). Exploit a healthy pool proportionally to its slack above threshold.\n     - Otherwise Cooperate (contribute just enough to keep the pool credible).\n   - **Punishment override:** if p_{t\u22121} dropped by more than 0.34 from p_{t\u22122} (mass defection detected), Defect for the next 2 rounds regardless of q, then resume the rules above.\n   - **Revival probe:** if I have defected for 4 consecutive rounds and t < r \u2212 E \u2212 3, Cooperate once to test whether the pool can be restarted; if p does not rise above \u03b8 within 2 rounds, return to defection.\n\n**Pseudocode:**\n\n```\nE = max(1, round(r/10)); theta = (k-1)/k\nt=0: play C; q = p_0\nfor t in 1 .. r-1:\n    if t >= r - E: play D; continue\n    if punish_timer > 0: play D; punish_timer -= 1; update q; continue\n    q = 0.6*q + 0.4*p_{t-1}\n    if p_{t-2} exists and p_{t-2} - p_{t-1} > 0.34:\n        punish_timer = 2; play D; continue\n    if q < theta:\n        if consec_D >= 4 and t < r - E - 3: play C (probe)\n        else: play D\n    else:\n        with prob min(0.5, q - theta + 0.15): play D\n        else: play C\n```\n\nTrack consec_D (consecutive own defections), resetting on any C.\n\n**Edge cases:** if r \u2264 3, cooperate in round 0 only, defect thereafter. If n = 2, treat p_t as the single opponent's move and set f = 0.25 fixed (exploiting one partner too hard kills the pool instantly)."

description_OPPORTUNISTIC_4 = "**Opportunistic Conditional Exploiter**\n\nNotation: m_t = number of opponents (out of n\u22121) who cooperated in round t; f_t = m_t/(n\u22121). Maintain a running exploitation flag and an estimate of opponent responsiveness.\n\n**Core idea:** Cooperate only when doing so plausibly sustains a high-cooperation environment worth harvesting; defect whenever cooperation levels are high enough to free-ride on, or too low to matter.\n\n**Decision rules (round t):**\n\n1. **Round 0:** Cooperate (probe; signal cooperativeness cheaply to seed reciprocators).\n\n2. **Endgame:** If t \u2265 r \u2212 E, defect unconditionally, where E = max(1, ceil(r/10)). No future to protect \u2014 pure extraction.\n\n3. **Middle rounds (1 \u2264 t < r \u2212 E):** Compute f = f_{t\u22121} and define thresholds L = (k\u22121)/(n\u22121) rescaled: use L_low = 0.3 and L_high = 0.7.\n   - **If f \u2265 L_high (rich commons):** Defect with probability p = 0.5, cooperate otherwise. You skim from a healthy pool while contributing just enough to keep conditional cooperators engaged. If after your defection f drops by more than 0.25, revert to cooperation next round (the crowd is watching \u2014 pay maintenance).\n   - **If L_low \u2264 f < L_high (fragile commons):** Cooperate \u2014 investment phase. Building cooperation now creates a bigger pool to exploit later.\n   - **If f < L_low (dead commons):** Defect. Exception: every ceil(r/8) rounds, cooperate once as a cheap revival probe; if f rises by \u2265 0.2 in response, treat as fragile commons next round; otherwise resume defecting.\n\n4. **Responsiveness test:** Track \u0394_t = f_t \u2212 f_{t\u22121} following your own action changes. If over the last 4 such observations opponents show no correlation with your play (|average \u0394| < 0.05 regardless of your action), classify opponents as **unresponsive** and defect for all remaining rounds \u2014 cooperation buys nothing.\n\n5. **Exploitation ratchet:** Maintain sucker count S = number of consecutive rounds where you defected while f \u2265 L_high stayed true. If S \u2265 3 (cooperation persists despite your defection), defect permanently until f falls below L_high \u2014 opponents are unconditional cooperators; milk them fully.\n\n**Pseudocode:**\n\n```\nif t == 0: play C\nelif t >= r - E: play D\nelif unresponsive: play D\nelse:\n    f = coop_fraction(t-1)\n    if f >= 0.7:\n        if sucker_streak >= 3: play D\n        elif last_defection_crashed_f: play C\n        else: play D with prob 0.5 else C\n    elif f >= 0.3: play C\n    else:\n        if t % ceil(r/8) == 0: play C  # revival probe\n        else: play D\n```"

description_OPPORTUNISTIC_5 = "**Opportunistic Threshold-Rider (\"Exploit-the-Crowd\")**\n\nCore idea: cooperate only when doing so is likely to sustain a cooperative pool worth milking; otherwise free-ride on whatever contributions exist.\n\nNotation: let m_t = number of *opponents* (out of n\u22121) who cooperated in round t. Define the profitability threshold T = \u2308(n\u22121)\u00b7(n\u2212k)/(k\u00b7(n\u22121))\u2309 \u2014 practically, use T = \u2308(n/k) \u2212 1\u2309, the minimum number of cooperating opponents such that a cooperative crowd is \"rich\" enough to be worth keeping alive.\n\n**Decision rules:**\n\n1. **Round 0:** Cooperate (cheap probe to seed conditional cooperators), unless r \u2264 2 or k/n \u2265 0.8 (near-guaranteed low marginal cost of defection anyway) \u2014 in those cases Defect.\n\n2. **Rounds 1 to r\u22121\u2212E (main phase):** maintain an exploitation counter and act on last round's m:\n   - If m_{t\u22121} \u2265 T (crowd is healthy): **Defect with probability p = 1/3, else Cooperate.** Track outcomes: if after your defection m does not drop by more than 1 the next round, increase p by 0.15 (cap 0.7) \u2014 the crowd is forgiving, milk harder. If m drops by \u2265 2, reset p to 1/3 and cooperate for the next 2 rounds to rebuild the pool.\n   - If \u2308(n\u22121)/3\u2309 \u2264 m_{t\u22121} < T (marginal crowd): Cooperate only if cooperation has been trending up (m_{t\u22121} > m_{t\u22122}); otherwise Defect.\n   - If m_{t\u22121} < \u2308(n\u22121)/3\u2309 (dead pool): **Defect.** Exception: every \u2308r/5\u2309 rounds, play one probing Cooperate to test whether cooperation can be reignited \u2014 but only if at least 4 rounds remain before the endgame.\n\n3. **Endgame (last E = max(1, \u2308r/10\u2309, 2) rounds): always Defect.** No future to protect \u2014 take everything.\n\n4. **Second-to-endgame guard:** in the round just before the endgame window, Defect if m_{t\u22121} < n\u22121 (assume others also endgame-defect; only cooperate off perfect unanimity, and even then only if p currently < 0.4).\n\n**Pseudocode:**\n\n```\nE = max(2, ceil(r/10)); T = ceil(n/k) - 1; p = 1/3; rebuild = 0\nfor t in 0..r-1:\n    if t >= r - E: play D\n    elif t == 0: play C if (r > 2 and k/n < 0.8) else D\n    elif rebuild > 0: play C; rebuild -= 1\n    elif m[t-1] >= T:\n        play D with prob p, else C\n        # after observing next round: adjust p as above\n    elif m[t-1] >= ceil((n-1)/3):\n        play C if m[t-1] > m[t-2] else D\n    else:\n        play C if (t % ceil(r/5) == 0 and t < r - E - 4) else D\n```\n\nUpdate rule after each round where you defected against a healthy crowd: `if m[t] >= m[t-1] - 1: p = min(0.7, p + 0.15) else: p = 1/3; rebuild = 2`."

description_OPPORTUNISTIC_6 = "**Opportunistic Threshold-Rider**\n\nCore idea: cooperate only when doing so is likely to sustain a cooperative pool worth exploiting; otherwise free-ride on it or abandon it.\n\nDefinitions:\n- m_t = number of *other* players who cooperated in round t (observed after each round).\n- coop_rate_t = m_t / (n\u22121).\n- Break-even threshold: my cooperation only pays if it maintains others' cooperation. Set T = ceil((n\u22121) \u00b7 (n/k \u2212 1) / (n\u22121))\u2026 simplified: require coop_rate \u2265 \u03b8 where \u03b8 = 1/k + 0.15 (capped at 0.9).\n\nDecision rules:\n\n1. **Round 0:** Cooperate. (Cheap probe that seeds conditional cooperators; needed to discover exploitable cooperators.)\n\n2. **Rounds 1 to r\u22121 (except endgame):**\n   - Let recent = coop_rate over last min(3, t) rounds (weighted 0.5/0.3/0.2, most recent first).\n   - **Exploit check:** If recent \u2265 0.8 for 2 consecutive rounds and I cooperated both times, defect this round (skim the pool), then return to normal rule. Do this at most once every 3 rounds \u2014 never defect-skim twice in a row while recent \u2265 0.8 (avoid collapsing the pool).\n   - **Otherwise:** Cooperate iff recent \u2265 \u03b8. Else defect.\n   - **Recovery probe:** If defecting for 4 consecutive rounds and t < r \u2212 max(4, r/5), cooperate once as a probe. If m_t after the probe fails to rise by \u2265 1 versus the prior round, do not probe again for another 6 rounds.\n\n3. **Endgame:** Defect unconditionally in the last L rounds, where L = max(1, floor(min(3, r/10)) + 1). I.e., always defect in the final round; defect earlier too when r is long, front-running opponents' endgame defection.\n\nPseudocode:\n\n```\n\u03b8 = min(0.9, 1/k + 0.15)\nL = max(1, min(3, floor(r/10)) + 1)\n\nif t == 0: play C\nelif t >= r - L: play D\nelse:\n    recent = weighted coop_rate of last 3 rounds\n    if recent >= 0.8 for last 2 rounds and I played C in both\n       and last skim was \u2265 3 rounds ago:\n        play D   # skim\n    elif recent >= \u03b8:\n        play C\n    else:\n        if 4 straight D's and probe allowed: play C  # probe\n        else: play D\n```\n\nTie-breaking: if recent is exactly \u03b8, cooperate only if m increased or held steady last round; otherwise defect."

description_OPPORTUNISTIC_7 = "**Opportunistic Threshold-Rider Strategy**\n\nCore idea: defect whenever the group sustains cooperation without me; contribute only when my cooperation is plausibly pivotal to keeping others cooperating.\n\nNotation: m = n \u2212 1 opponents; coop_t = number of opponents who cooperated in round t; frac_t = coop_t / m. My cooperation is only worth it if it sustains at least ~n/k extra cooperators in future rounds.\n\n**Decision rules:**\n\n1. **Round 0:** Cooperate (probe/seed cooperation cheaply \u2014 many strategies are reciprocal, and cooperating first unlocks exploitable cooperators).\n\n2. **Endgame:** Defect in the last L rounds unconditionally, where L = max(1, floor(r/10)). No future to leverage, so cash out \u2014 and start slightly before the crowd.\n\n3. **Middle rounds t (1 \u2264 t < r \u2212 L):**\n   - Compute recent cooperation: f = frac over the last min(3, t) rounds (weighted 0.5/0.3/0.2 most-recent-first, or simple average if fewer rounds).\n   - **Free-ride zone:** if f \u2265 0.6, defect \u2014 cooperation is self-sustaining; harvest it.\n   - **Dead zone:** if f < 0.25, defect \u2014 the pool is dead; contributing is throwing money away.\n   - **Pivotal zone (0.25 \u2264 f < 0.6):** cooperate only if my last action seems to move others, i.e. run a responsiveness check:\n     - Maintain estimate \u03c1 = correlation between my action in round t\u22121 and change in coop_t (track: avg \u0394coop after my C minus avg \u0394coop after my D over history).\n     - Cooperate if \u03c1 > 1/(k/n\u00b71) equivalent test \u2014 concretely, cooperate if \u03c1 \u00d7 (k/n) \u00d7 (remaining rounds before endgame, capped at 5) > (1 \u2212 k/n); otherwise defect.\n     - Before enough data (fewer than 3 observations of each of my actions), cooperate in this zone by default.\n\n4. **Milking cycle guard:** if I've defected for 3+ consecutive rounds while f is declining by more than 0.1 per round, cooperate once (a \"re-seed\") \u2014 but only if t < r \u2212 L \u2212 3 (enough rounds left to profit from a revival). Never re-seed twice within 4 rounds if the first re-seed produced no rebound (\u0394coop \u2264 0).\n\n5. **Exploitation detection:** if my cooperation rate over the last 5 rounds exceeds f + 0.3 (I'm giving more than the group), defect for the next 2 rounds regardless of zone.\n\n**Pseudocode:**\n\n```\nif t == 0: play C\nelif t >= r - L: play D\nelse:\n    f = weighted_recent_frac(last 3 rounds)\n    if my_coop_rate(last 5) > f + 0.3: play D  # being exploited\n    elif f >= 0.6: play D                       # free-ride\n    elif f < 0.25:\n        if reseed_conditions_met(): play C      # milking guard\n        else: play D\n    else:                                       # pivotal zone\n        if insufficient_data or responsiveness_worthwhile(): play C\n        else: play D\n```\n\nThe strategy never cooperates out of fairness \u2014 every C is an investment made only when history suggests it buys back more than 1 \u2212 k/n per round in induced future contributions, and all investment stops before the final rounds so gains are banked, not reciprocated away."

description_OPPORTUNISTIC_8 = "**Opportunistic Threshold-Rider Strategy**\n\nCore idea: defect whenever others' cooperation is high enough to free-ride on, cooperate only when needed to keep a fragile cooperative equilibrium alive \u2014 and always defect at the end.\n\nDefinitions:\n- m_t = number of opponents (out of n\u22121) who cooperated in round t.\n- f_t = m_t / (n\u22121), opponents' cooperation rate.\n- Endgame length E = max(1, ceil(0.1\u00b7r)) but at least the final 2 rounds if r \u2265 4.\n\nDecision rules for round t:\n\n1. **Endgame:** If t \u2265 r \u2212 E, play D unconditionally.\n\n2. **Round 0:** Play C (probe/seed cooperation cheaply) \u2014 unless r \u2264 3, in which case play D.\n\n3. **Round 1:** If f_0 \u2265 0.5, play D (exploit the crowd); else play C once more if f_0 > 0, otherwise D.\n\n4. **Rounds 2 \u2264 t < r \u2212 E:** Let f = f_{t-1} and f_prev = f_{t-2}.\n   - If f \u2265 0.6: play D \u2014 cooperation is robust, free-ride.\n   - If f < 0.25: play D \u2014 public good is dead, don't waste endowment.\n   - If 0.25 \u2264 f < 0.6 (fragile zone):\n     - If f < f_prev (cooperation is declining): play C to prop it up.\n     - Else: play C with probability 0.5, D otherwise (contribute just enough to sustain, skim the rest).\n\n5. **Collapse lockout:** If f_{t-1} < 0.25 for 3 consecutive rounds, defect for the remainder of the game (no revival attempts), except: if a later round shows f \u2265 0.6 spontaneously, resume rule 4.\n\n6. **Exploitation cap:** Track own cooperation count. Never let own cooperation rate exceed the observed average opponent rate \u2014 if it would, override rule 4's C with D that round.\n\nPseudocode:\n\n```\nif t >= r - E: return D\nif t == 0: return C if r > 3 else D\nif t == 1: return D if f0 >= 0.5 else (C if f0 > 0 else D)\n\nf = coop_rate(t-1)\nif locked_out and f < 0.6: return D\nif f >= 0.6: return D\nif f < 0.25: update lockout counter; return D\n# fragile zone\nif my_coop_rate >= avg_opp_coop_rate: return D\nif f < coop_rate(t-2): return C\nreturn C with prob 0.5 else D\n```"

description_INDIVIDUALISTIC_1 = "**Strategy: Exploitative Threshold Reciprocator**\n\nCore idea: cooperate only when doing so is likely to sustain enough opponent cooperation that the returned share exceeds the kept endowment; otherwise free-ride.\n\nDefinitions:\n- m = n \u2212 1 opponents; coop_t = number of opponents who cooperated in round t.\n- Cooperation is personally profitable only if it induces/sustains behavior; my own contribution returns k/n < 1, so I contribute only as an investment in others' continued cooperation.\n- Threshold T = ceil(m \u00d7 (n \u2212 k) / (k \u00d7 (m))) simplified: use T = ceil((n/k) \u2212 1), the minimum number of cooperating opponents needed so that (k/n)(coop+1) \u2265 1, i.e., mutual cooperation beats universal defection for me.\n\nDecision rules:\n\n1. **Round 0:** Cooperate (probe: signal willingness to elicit conditional cooperators).\n\n2. **Rounds 1 to r\u22121 (except endgame):**\n   - Maintain forgiveness counter f, initially 1.\n   - If coop_{t\u22121} \u2265 T: Cooperate.\n   - Else if coop_{t\u22121} \u2265 ceil(T/2) and f > 0: Cooperate once, decrement f (attempt to restart cooperation).\n   - Else: Defect.\n   - Reset f to 1 whenever coop in some round reaches \u2265 T (population proved responsive).\n\n3. **Exploitation check:** Track my average payoff while cooperating vs. while defecting over the last min(5, t) rounds each. If the defecting average exceeds the cooperating average and coop levels are flat or rising regardless of my action (|coop_{t\u22121} \u2212 coop_{t\u22122}| \u2264 1 after I switched actions), the population is unconditional \u2014 defect permanently (they don't respond to me, so contribution is pure loss).\n\n4. **Endgame:** Defect in the final round unconditionally. Defect in the last E = max(1, floor(log2(r))) rounds capped at 3 \u2014 i.e., defect in rounds r\u22121, and also r\u22122 (and r\u22123 if r \u2265 20), since opponents' incentive to punish vanishes and my contribution can no longer buy future cooperation.\n\nPseudocode:\n\n```\nE = 1 if r < 8 else (2 if r < 20 else 3)\nT = ceil(n/k) - 1\nf = 1; locked_defect = False\n\nfor t in 0..r-1:\n    if t >= r - E or locked_defect: play D; continue\n    if t == 0: play C; continue\n    if coop[t-1] >= T:\n        play C; f = 1\n    elif coop[t-1] >= ceil(T/2) and f > 0:\n        play C; f -= 1\n    else:\n        play D\n    # after observing round: run exploitation check (rule 3);\n    # if triggered, locked_defect = True\n```\n\nEdge cases: if T \u2264 0 (very high k), cooperate whenever coop_{t\u22121} \u2265 1, defect otherwise after the probe. If T \u2265 m (k near 1), cooperation is nearly worthless \u2014 defect from round 1 onward after the initial probe unless coop_0 = m."

description_INDIVIDUALISTIC_2 = "**Strategy: Exploitative Conditional Free-Rider**\n\nCore idea: cooperate only when my contribution is plausibly pivotal to sustaining a cooperative pool I can harvest; otherwise defect and pocket others' contributions.\n\nNotation: at round t, let m_{t-1} = number of opponents (out of n\u22121) who cooperated last round, and f = m_{t-1}/(n\u22121). Let threshold T = k/n (my marginal return per cooperator; since k < n, my own cooperation is always a per-round loss, so I cooperate only strategically to keep others cooperating).\n\nDecision rules:\n\n1. **Round 0:** Cooperate (cheap signal to seed cooperation I can later exploit).\n2. **Endgame:** Defect unconditionally in the last L = max(1, floor(r/10)) rounds \u2014 no future to protect, take the money.\n3. **Middle rounds (1 \u2264 t < r \u2212 L):**\n   - Maintain an exploitation counter. Alternate between \"seeding\" and \"harvesting\":\n     - If f \u2265 2/3: opponents cooperate robustly \u2192 **Defect** (harvest; they don't need me).\n     - If 1/3 \u2264 f < 2/3: cooperation is fragile \u2192 **Cooperate**, but only if I did not cooperate in the previous two rounds while f stayed in this band and didn't rise (i.e., my cooperation is having no effect); in that stalled case, **Defect**.\n     - If f < 1/3: pool is dead \u2192 **Defect** (contributing is pure loss).\n   - **Occasional probe:** if I've defected for 4 consecutive rounds while f \u2265 2/3 and f is declining monotonically over those rounds, cooperate for one round to prop the pool back up, then resume the rules above.\n4. **Collapse lock:** if f < 1/3 for 3 consecutive rounds, switch to permanent defection for the rest of the game (no more seeding \u2014 sunk cost).\n\nPseudocode:\n\n```\nif t == 0: play C\nelif t >= r - L: play D\nelif collapsed: play D\nelif f >= 2/3:\n    if last 4 of my moves == D and f declined 4 rounds straight: play C\n    else: play D\nelif f >= 1/3:\n    if my last two moves were C and f did not increase: play D\n    else: play C\nelse: play D\nupdate collapsed flag\n```\n\nEvery cooperation is an investment made solely to keep others contributing so I can defect against them; whenever their cooperation is either self-sustaining or hopeless, I defect and maximize my own take."

description_INDIVIDUALISTIC_3 = "**Strategy: Exploitative Threshold Defector**\n\nCore principle: cooperation only pays me if it induces enough others to cooperate; my own contribution costs 1 and returns only k/n < 1 to me. So default to D, and cooperate only as a calculated investment to sustain others' cooperation.\n\nDefinitions:\n- m_t = number of opponents (out of n\u22121) who cooperated in round t.\n- threshold T = ceil((n\u22121) \u00b7 (n\u2212k)/(k\u00b7(n\u22121)))  \u2014 roughly, cooperate only when the group is highly cooperative; in practice use T = ceil(0.6\u00b7(n\u22121)).\n- E = number of endgame rounds: E = max(1, floor(r/10)) + 1... simplified: defect in the last 2 rounds (last 1 if r \u2264 3).\n\nDecision rules:\n\n1. **Round 0:** Play C (probe; signals cooperativeness cheaply and gathers information).\n\n2. **Endgame (last 2 rounds, or last round if r \u2264 3):** Play D unconditionally. No future to invest in \u2014 contribution is a pure loss.\n\n3. **Middle rounds:** maintain a \"trust score\" and exploit periodically:\n   - Play C in round t if m_{t\u22121} \u2265 T (group is cooperative enough that my defection risks collapsing a stream worth more than 1 per round to me), **except**:\n     - Every 4th round in which I would cooperate, play D instead (periodic exploitation: pocket the extra 1\u2212k/n while the group's momentum likely persists, since opponents can't identify me).\n     - If m dropped by more than 2 immediately after one of my exploitation defections, suspend exploitation (skip the every-4th defection) for the next 8 rounds \u2014 the group is punishing aggregate defection, so exploitation is too costly.\n   - Play D if m_{t\u22121} < T.\n\n4. **Re-probe:** If I have played D for 5 consecutive rounds and at least 5 non-endgame rounds remain, play C once. If m rises above T within 2 rounds, resume rule 3; otherwise return to D and double the wait before the next probe (5 \u2192 10 \u2192 20 \u2026).\n\nPseudocode:\n\n```\nif t == 0: play C\nelif t >= r - (2 if r > 3 else 1): play D\nelif m[t-1] >= T:\n    if exploit_counter % 4 == 3 and not exploit_suspended: play D\n    else: play C\n    exploit_counter += 1\nelse:\n    if consecutive_D >= probe_wait and rounds_left >= 5:\n        play C; probe_wait *= 2\n    else: play D\n```\n\nEvery choice maximizes my own payoff: cooperation is used solely as bait/maintenance for a public-good stream I can skim, defection is the default whenever the group can't sustain returns exceeding my contribution cost, and the endgame is harvested unconditionally."

description_INDIVIDUALISTIC_4 = "**Strategy: Opportunistic Conditional Exploiter**\n\nCore idea: cooperate only when it demonstrably raises my own expected payoff by sustaining others' contributions; otherwise defect and free-ride.\n\nDefinitions:\n- m = n \u2212 1 opponents; coop_t = number of opponents who cooperated in round t.\n- f_t = coop_t / m (opponent cooperation rate last round).\n- Threshold \u03b8 = (n \u2212 k) / (k(n\u22121)) \u2014 the fraction of opponents whose continued cooperation must plausibly hinge on mine for cooperating to pay. Cap \u03b8 at 0.5 minimum: \u03b8* = max(\u03b8, 0.5).\n\nDecision rules:\n\n1. **Round 0:** Cooperate (probe; cheap signal to encourage conditional cooperators).\n\n2. **Endgame:** Defect unconditionally in the last L = max(1, \u23080.1\u00b7r\u2309) rounds. Cooperation cannot yield future returns there.\n\n3. **Middle rounds (1 \u2264 t < r \u2212 L):**\n   - Maintain an exponentially weighted cooperation estimate: F \u2190 0.6\u00b7f_{t\u22121} + 0.4\u00b7F (initialize F = f_0).\n   - If F \u2265 \u03b8*: cooperate \u2014 the crowd is responsive enough that fueling it pays via future rounds.\n   - If F < \u03b8*: defect.\n   - **Exploitation pulse:** even when F \u2265 \u03b8*, defect once every 5th eligible round (i.e., if t mod 5 == 4), skimming free-rider profit while cooperation is high. Skip the pulse if F < \u03b8* + 0.15 (fragile cooperation \u2014 don't destabilize your income stream).\n   - **Dead pool lock:** if F < 0.2 for two consecutive rounds, switch to permanent defection for the rest of the game (no revival attempts \u2014 probes cost more than they return).\n   - **Revival probe:** if not locked and I've defected 3 consecutive rounds while F \u2208 [0.2, \u03b8*), cooperate once to test whether reciprocators respond; return to the rule above next round.\n\nPseudocode:\n\n```\nif t == 0: play C\nelif t >= r - L or locked: play D\nelse:\n    F = 0.6*f_prev + 0.4*F\n    if F < 0.2 two rounds running: locked = True; play D\n    elif F >= \u03b8*:\n        if t % 5 == 4 and F >= \u03b8* + 0.15: play D   # skim\n        else: play C\n    elif F >= 0.2 and my_last_3 == DDD: play C      # probe\n    else: play D\n```\n\nEvery cooperation is an investment in others' future contributions; every defection harvests the public good others fund. When neither pays, defect \u2014 the safe private payoff is always mine."

description_INDIVIDUALISTIC_5 = "**Strategy: Opportunistic Conditional Contributor (OCC)**\n\nCore principle: cooperate only when doing so plausibly sustains others' cooperation worth more to me than the 1\u2212k/n I sacrifice; otherwise defect and free-ride.\n\nDefinitions:\n- m_t = number of opponents (out of n\u22121) who cooperated in round t.\n- Cooperation is personally profitable only via its effect on future opponent behavior, so all decisions weigh expected future returns to me alone.\n- Threshold T = ceil((n\u22121) \u00d7 (1 \u2212 k/n)). Intuition: I only \"invest\" in the group when opponent cooperation is high enough that keeping it alive pays me back.\n\n**Decision rules:**\n\n1. **Round 0:** Cooperate (probe \u2014 cheap signal to seed conditional cooperators, but only if r \u2265 4 and k/n \u2265 0.4; otherwise defect).\n\n2. **Rounds 1 to r\u22121 (except endgame, below):**\n   - Compute recent cooperation: m = m_{t\u22121}.\n   - If m \u2265 T: **Cooperate** \u2014 the pool is rich enough that sustaining it beats free-riding it into collapse.\n   - If m < T but m \u2265 T/2 and I defected last round: **Cooperate** once as a rebuild attempt, at most once every 3 rounds. Track rebuild attempts; if two consecutive rebuild attempts fail to raise m, permanently stop rebuilding.\n   - Otherwise: **Defect.**\n\n3. **Exploitation pulse:** Even when m \u2265 T, defect with probability p = 0.1 (or once every 10 rounds deterministically) to skim extra payoff, provided m \u2265 T + 1 (surplus cushion so my lapse is unlikely to trigger collapse). Skip the pulse if m == T exactly.\n\n4. **Endgame:** Let E = max(1, round(0.15 \u00d7 r)) but cap E at 3. In the final E rounds, **always defect** \u2014 no future rounds exist for cooperation to buy anything, so keep the endowment. Additionally, in round r\u2212E\u22121, defect if m_{t\u22121} < T + 1 (start unraveling early against fragile groups).\n\n5. **Collapse lock:** If m_{t\u22121} = 0 for two consecutive rounds, defect for the remainder of the game (population is hostile; cooperation is pure loss).\n\n**Pseudocode:**\n\n```\nT = ceil((n-1)*(1 - k/n)); E = min(3, max(1, round(0.15*r)))\nif t == 0: play C if (r >= 4 and k/n >= 0.4) else D\nelif t >= r - E: play D\nelif last_two_rounds_m == 0: play D forever\nelif m >= T:\n    if m >= T+1 and pulse_due(): play D   # skim\n    else: play C\nelif m >= T/2 and my_last == D and rebuild_allowed(): play C\nelse: play D\n```\n\nEvery cooperative move is an investment expected to return more than its cost to me personally; every defection captures immediate private gain when the future no longer pays."

description_INDIVIDUALISTIC_6 = "**Strategy: Exploitative Threshold Reciprocator**\n\nCore idea: cooperate only when it is instrumentally profitable \u2014 i.e., when past evidence suggests enough opponents condition their cooperation on the group's cooperation level that my contribution sustains a stream of future contributions worth more than the 1 \u2212 k/n it costs me. Otherwise, defect and free-ride.\n\nNotation: m = n \u2212 1 opponents. After round t, observe coop_t = number of cooperating opponents. Let f_t = coop_t / m. Define endgame length E = max(1, ceil(n/k)) \u2014 the final E rounds are unconditional defection since no future can repay a contribution.\n\n**Decision rules:**\n\n1. **Round 0:** Cooperate (probe: signals conditional cooperation to reciprocators at cost at most 1 \u2212 k/n).\n\n2. **Final E rounds (t \u2265 r \u2212 E):** Defect always.\n\n3. **Middle rounds (1 \u2264 t < r \u2212 E):** Maintain a running exponentially weighted cooperation rate:\n   - w_t = 0.6 \u00b7 f_{t\u22121} + 0.4 \u00b7 w_{t\u22121}, with w_1 = f_0.\n   \n   Cooperate iff **both**:\n   - w_t \u2265 n/(k\u00b7m)  \u2014 expected opponent contributions triggered/sustained exceed my net cost, assuming roughly reciprocal opponents; equivalently k\u00b7(1 + w_t\u00b7m)/n > 1 plus continuation value; and\n   - f_{t\u22121} \u2265 f_{t\u22122} \u2212 1/m when t \u2265 2 (cooperation is not collapsing).\n   \n   Otherwise defect.\n\n4. **Punishment/exploitation lock:** If I defect for 2 consecutive middle rounds while w_t stays below threshold, stay in defection until f_{t\u22121} strictly exceeds n/(k\u00b7m) (opponents rebuilt cooperation without me \u2014 rejoin only to keep reciprocators contributing).\n\n5. **Periodic exploitation test:** Every 5th cooperative round (count of my own C plays \u2261 0 mod 5), defect once regardless of w_t. If f drops by more than 1/m in the following round compared to before the test, opponents are responsive \u2014 resume rule 3. If f is unchanged, opponents are unconditional cooperators: **defect permanently** for the rest of the game and free-ride.\n\n6. **Re-probe:** If locked in defection (rule 4) and more than 6 rounds remain before the endgame, and f_{t\u22121} \u2265 0.5, play one exploratory C to test whether cooperation can be reignited; return to rule 3 with reset w_t = f_{t\u22121}.\n\n```\nif t >= r - E: play D\nelif t == 0: play C\nelif in_permanent_defect (rule 5 triggered): play D\nelif exploitation_test_due: play D; evaluate response next round\nelif defect_lock and not reprobe_condition: play D\nelif w_t >= n/(k*m) and cooperation not collapsing: play C\nelse: play D\n```\n\nEvery cooperative act is an investment expected to return more than its cost in induced opponent contributions; the moment that expectation fails \u2014 unresponsive opponents, collapsing cooperation, or no remaining future \u2014 defect and pocket the endowment."

description_INDIVIDUALISTIC_7 = "**Strategy: \"Exploitative Threshold Shadow\"**\n\nCore idea: cooperate only when doing so is likely to sustain enough others' cooperation that my share of the public good exceeds my private endowment; otherwise free-ride.\n\nDefinitions:\n- m_t = number of opponents (out of n\u22121) who cooperated in round t.\n- Break-even cooperators needed for C to beat D given my own contribution: cooperating costs me 1 \u2212 k/n; it pays only if it keeps others cooperating in the future. So the decision is forward-looking, not per-round.\n- coop_rate_t = m_t / (n\u22121).\n- Endgame length: E = max(1, ceil(k)) final rounds.\n\nDecision rules:\n\n1. **Round 0:** Cooperate (probe for reciprocators) \u2014 unless r \u2264 2 or k/n is very high anyway; specifically, defect in round 0 if r \u2264 2.\n\n2. **Endgame (last E rounds, t \u2265 r \u2212 E):** Always defect. No future to influence, so D strictly dominates.\n\n3. **Middle rounds (1 \u2264 t < r \u2212 E):** Maintain a smoothed cooperation estimate:\n   - q \u2190 0.6 \u00d7 coop_rate_{t\u22121} + 0.4 \u00d7 q_prev (initialize q = coop_rate_0).\n   - Cooperate iff q \u2265 \u03b8, where \u03b8 = (n \u2212 k) / (k(n \u2212 1)) \u2014 the fraction of cooperating opponents at which mutual cooperation strictly beats universal defection with margin \u2014 capped into [0.4, 0.8].\n   - **Exploitation probe:** even when q \u2265 \u03b8, defect with probability p = 0.1 every round, and always defect in one scheduled round t = floor((r\u2212E)/2), to skim free-rider profit; anonymity means this rarely triggers targeted punishment.\n   - **Forgiveness test:** if I've defected for 3+ consecutive rounds due to q < \u03b8, play C once every 5 rounds as a cheap signal to check whether cooperation can be re-seeded (skip this if fewer than 5 rounds remain before endgame).\n\n4. **Collapse detection:** if m_t = 0 for two consecutive rounds, set q = 0 and defect until a forgiveness test shows m_t \u2265 ceil(\u03b8(n\u22121)); if the test fails twice, defect permanently.\n\nPseudocode:\n```\nE = max(1, ceil(k)); theta = clamp((n-k)/(k*(n-1)), 0.4, 0.8)\nt=0: play C if r>2 else D\neach t>=1:\n  q = 0.6*rate(t-1) + 0.4*q\n  if t >= r-E: play D\n  elif collapsed and not forgiveness_round: play D\n  elif q >= theta:\n      play D with prob 0.1 or if t == floor((r-E)/2), else C\n  else:\n      play C if forgiveness_round else D\n```"

description_INDIVIDUALISTIC_8 = "**Strategy: Exploitative Conditional Defector**\n\nCore principle: maximize own payoff; cooperate only when doing so is likely to sustain enough others' cooperation that my share of the induced public good exceeds the 1 \u2212 k/n cost of contributing. Otherwise free-ride.\n\nDefinitions:\n- coop_t = number of opponents (out of n\u22121) who cooperated in round t.\n- threshold T = ceil((n\u22121) \u00d7 (n\u2212k)/k) \u2014 minimum opponent cooperators such that reciprocal cooperation plausibly pays; but cap: if T > n\u22121, always defect.\n- E = min(3, ceil(r/10)) endgame rounds.\n\nDecision rules:\n\n1. **Round 0:** Defect. (Free option to probe; keeps endowment while sampling population.)\n\n2. **Endgame (last E rounds, and always the final round):** Defect unconditionally \u2014 no future to leverage.\n\n3. **Middle rounds (1 \u2264 t < r \u2212 E):**\n   - Compute recent cooperation: avg over last min(3, t) rounds of coop.\n   - If avg \u2265 T (i.e., cooperation is high enough that conditional cooperators dominate and my defection risks collapsing a stream worth more than the per-round free-ride gain): **Cooperate**, except:\n     - **Probe defections:** every 5th cooperative round (counter of my own cooperations), defect once to skim extra payoff; if coop level drops by more than 25% in the following round, stop probing for the rest of the game.\n   - If avg < T: **Defect.**\n   - **Re-entry test:** if I have defected for 4 consecutive rounds and t < r \u2212 E \u2212 3, cooperate once as a signal probe; if coop_{t+1} > coop_t, resume the conditional rule; otherwise defect for another 4 rounds before probing again.\n\n4. **Collapse lock:** if avg cooperation over the last 5 rounds < 0.5 opponents, defect for the remainder (population is hopeless; contribution is pure loss).\n\nPseudocode:\n\n```\nif t == 0 or t >= r - E: play D\nelif locked_out: play D\nelse:\n    avg = mean(coop over last min(3,t) rounds)\n    if last5_avg < 0.5 and t >= 5: locked_out = True; play D\n    elif avg >= T:\n        my_coop_count += 1\n        if probing_enabled and my_coop_count % 5 == 0: play D  # skim\n        else: play C\n    else:\n        consec_D += 1\n        if consec_D >= 4 and t < r - E - 3: play C (probe); consec_D = 0\n        else: play D\n```\n\nEvery cooperation is instrumental \u2014 a payment to keep others contributing; every defection captures the private unit whenever the future revenue from cooperation cannot justify the cost."
